1
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:24,024
Last night, I was tossing
and turning like nobody's business.

2
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:27,694
Not sure how long I actually slept.
Maybe got, like, four hours at best.

3
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:32,365
Dawn of the final day.

4
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,622
I really want to win this thing.

5
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:42,417
Honestly, when I first got here,

6
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,462
I was pretty blown away
at the caliber of all my competitors.

7
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:49,049
But everybody was kinda already familiar
with one another from previous stuff,

8
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:52,719
so I sorta felt like I started
with a huge disadvantage.

9
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,596
Hyun Kyung-lyul.

10
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:56,598
-It's one.
-That is correct.

11
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:59,350
So with all the odds like that against me,

12
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:03,354
I had to really prove myself and show
both my ability and my earnestness.

13
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:05,273
-So is this four-on-two now?
-At this point,

14
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:07,984
-I'm playing the way I want.
-You know what, I can respect that.

15
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:11,154
That's basically how I've been
getting through each day,

16
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:15,742
and I'd like to think I've demonstrated
both my will to survive and my sheer grit.

17
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:29,506
The reason there's so much pressure on me…

18
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:31,674
<i>As the player in first place,</i>
<i>Jang Dong-min…</i>

19
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,760
<i>As the player in first place,</i>
<i>Jang Dong-min…</i>

20
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:35,804
<i>As the player in first place,</i>
<i>Jang Dong-min…</i>

21
00:01:35,887 --> 00:01:38,098
<i>As the player in first place,</i>
<i>Jang Dong-min…</i>

22
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,766
<i>As the winner, Jang Dong-min…</i>

23
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,392
Jang Dong-min wins.

24
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:45,105
Well, it's the fact
that I've won every single round so far.

25
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:46,898
A lot of viewers say,

26
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:49,818
"If you team up with Jang Dong-min,
you might survive, sure,

27
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:53,113
but it's just a matter of the order
in which you'll be eliminated."

28
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:56,616
And whether you'll team up with
or face off against one another,

29
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:59,536
at the end of the day,
there can only be one true winner.

30
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,996
And yeah, the pressure
of having gotten here

31
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,124
without a single loss
is pretty overwhelming.

32
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:07,001
But that's all the more reason
I can't allow myself to lose.

33
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,087
I realized right after
the very first game.

34
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:12,882
If you stay beneath Dong-min's shadow,
you'll never rise above him.

35
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,259
That was the whole point of doing this.

36
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:16,970
Yeah, and I bid three Pieces
specifically to stop that from happening.

37
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:19,973
And I knew that I was gonna
have to figure out how to beat him

38
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:22,517
if I wanted any shot
at winning this thing.

39
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,644
Each day, with each game,

40
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,188
I was carefully analyzing
all of his strategies,

41
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:30,024
slowly but surely figuring out
how I could beat him

42
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,651
right here on the final stage.

43
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:35,363
I noticed Kyung-lyul
sought me out right from the beginning

44
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,824
when we were playing Either Or
on the first day.

45
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:39,242
He's a driven kind of guy.

46
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:42,495
Even if somebody gave me
the right answer, why trust 'em?

47
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,706
When we're choosing between
the greater good and personal gain…

48
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:46,291
-Nothing you can do.
-Mm-hmm.

49
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:48,334
I've already submitted number two,
so that's that.

50
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,794
Oh, yeah, sure.

51
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:54,632
He and I really clashed
quite a bit on this show.

52
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,969
-Hey, buy… What was it again? What was it?
-Steel.

53
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,387
Yeah, buy 50 shares of Steel. Come on.

54
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,973
-Gonna save me if I do this?
-Yeah, just do it.

55
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:03,349
Then it's XITSUH.

56
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,560
-That's gotta be the middle ground.
-Not cool with that.

57
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:07,604
How am I supposed to negotiate like this?

58
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:10,106
Maybe competing bidders
shouldn't be negotiating at all?

59
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,774
-He could read me if I say a word.
-Yeah.

60
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,194
You've bid one three-won coin.

61
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,821
A five-won coin and a one-won coin
for a total of six won.

62
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:18,323
I'm not too confident in this game.

63
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,658
Hey, I told you
not to think like that, didn't I?

64
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:23,328
This is a battle of wits.
Have confidence in yourself.

65
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:25,246
Here is the hidden word.

66
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,623
Huh?

67
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:29,000
-Hyun Kyung-lyul wins two points.
-"Hair."

68
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,711
Hey, when it comes to adding
more prize money? I'm all for it.

69
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:34,130
This all comes down to your choice,
to pick personal gain…

70
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:35,882
I have no other choice but to pick it.

71
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:39,302
Hate to say this, but I think
Jang Dong-min has no weaknesses

72
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:40,553
that I can spot.

73
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:43,598
But all I have to do is be
just a tiny bit better than him today.

74
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:47,352
And some people might say that's like
trying to break a rock with an egg, but…

75
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,979
You know what I'd tell them?
That I'm a super egg.

76
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:53,191
I'm a super egg that's gonna
find a way to break a rock.

77
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,484
It's like in school

78
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:57,820
when you meet that one kid who always
gets a perfect score on their tests,

79
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,739
but then they get one question wrong?

80
00:03:59,822 --> 00:04:01,241
It's like the ultimate shame.

81
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:04,035
I'm that kid with the perfect score.
Only difference?

82
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:05,495
I'm not missin' nothin'.

83
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:23,846
Even yesterday, it felt like
this would go on forever…

84
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:28,184
Not today. It feels more like
the first day all over again.

85
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:30,561
I'm almost kind of sad.
I wish it could keep going.

86
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:32,355
I know, right?

87
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:33,731
-Oh.
-Hey, who's that?

88
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:34,816
Hey!

89
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:36,901
JOHN PARK,13TH ELIMINATED PLAYER
JAE JAE, 13TH ELIMINATED PLAYER

90
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,654
Well, look at you guys,
dressed to the nines again. Damn.

91
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:42,282
-You're the first to arrive.
-I always knew you guys would make it.

92
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:45,285
-JAE JAE, I was sad to see you go.
-Ugh, it happens.

93
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:47,120
-I was so bummed.
-Dude.

94
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:48,663
-Hey, Park!
-Lookin' sharp.

95
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:51,666
-Tell me both of you slept.
-No, haven't slept a wink, to be honest.

96
00:04:51,749 --> 00:04:53,501
I had so many nightmares.

97
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:56,212
-What about you guys?
-I went and knocked back a beer.

98
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,547
-Oh, yeah?
-Yeah.

99
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,215
Man, wish you and I could have shared one.

100
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:00,341
-Aw.
-Right?

101
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,468
-Ah, well, that would've been nice too.
-Yeah.

102
00:05:02,552 --> 00:05:05,847
Hey, be honest. You were tossing
in your sleep all night, weren't you?

103
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:08,516
-"Why did I submit black zero?"
-Just the one.

104
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,768
There was just one.

105
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:12,645
-The one thing I'll never live down.
-Yeah.

106
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,731
I won't lie, there was a little bit
of that on my mind.

107
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:17,400
Yeah, I think that'll haunt you for,
like, three months.

108
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,571
Three months, you'll be like,
"Why did I do that?"

109
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,657
"Why the hell did
I run that stupid bluff?"

110
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,576
-It hurts! Oh, well.
-This was fun, though.

111
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:28,161
I'll learn to live with it.

112
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:29,495
-Oh!
-Who is it?

113
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,999
JUNG WON-YOUNG, 12TH ELIMINATED
XITSUH, 11TH ELIMINATED

114
00:05:33,082 --> 00:05:35,418
Reporting. Congrats to whoever
I'm congratulating.

115
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:37,211
-So which one?
-These two right here.

116
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:40,006
Oh! So proud of you, my dudes.

117
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,133
-I knew you would make it this far.
-XITSUH.

118
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:43,301
-Thanks.
-Who do you think it is?

119
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:44,385
Hell yeah.

120
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,678
-Oh, boy.
-Of course.

121
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:47,305
Wonder which two are the finalists?

122
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,433
-Nah.
-Proud of you.

123
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,393
Dude, Park.

124
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:54,479
-What even happened?
-Well, I tried the best I could,

125
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:55,563
-but you know.
-Man.

126
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:56,939
Prison Match messed you up?

127
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:58,191
Yeah, I lost that one.

128
00:05:58,274 --> 00:05:59,650
You guys beat the king of the prison.

129
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:00,777
-Mmm.
-We did.

130
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,278
He was our boss in there.

131
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:04,030
Yeah, he beat the prison zombie.

132
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:06,115
Oh, yeah. He's king of the exile zone.

133
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,994
Yo, I'm king of the exile zone.

134
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:11,454
-You can have it.
-Sure.

135
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:14,290
-He closed the shutters on the exile zone.
-Whatever, I spent three nights in there.

136
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,250
-I was there too.
-I got a question.

137
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:17,919
-What's that?
-Why are there still two?

138
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,505
-Ah…
-Dude, why do you think?

139
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:23,800
When I came back from the hidden stage,
I chose to take Pieces,

140
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:27,303
and when we were down to the final five,
nobody picked the hundred million won.

141
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:29,222
Aw… And we got a choice between

142
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:31,599
-greater good and personal gain again.
-Got another Either Or.

143
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:35,144
-The greater good is truly dead.
-I wanted to pick the greater good too.

144
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,604
But we had the same conversation again.

145
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:38,689
Even after all that,
they still didn't want to do it.

146
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:41,901
If you'd kept me alive, you could've
had an extra 200 mil stacked up.

147
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:43,861
-That's right.
-What a shame.

148
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,781
YURISA,10TH ELIMINATED
KIM DONG-JAE, 9TH ELIMINATED

149
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:47,865
-Check it out.
-Hey, guys.

150
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:50,326
-Welcome back.
-Good to see you all.

151
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:51,994
We didn't even get
to say goodbye properly.

152
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:54,247
-Hey!
-Congratulations, guys.

153
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:56,874
Ah, I knew it would be you two. Geez.

154
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,835
I could just tell by your outfits.

155
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,962
-Dong-jae.
-I can tell by your outfit.

156
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,506
Oh, it's down to the two of you.

157
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,591
Nah, Dong-jae, it's the two of us, duh.

158
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:08,344
Oh, yeah, with those outfits?
It's obviously you two…

159
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:09,554
Yeah, our colors match.

160
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:11,472
-Dong-min's agreed to be our waiter today.
-Yeah, right?

161
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:13,516
These two are serving hors d'oeuvres.

162
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,268
-Oh, of course.
-Oh, thank you.

163
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:17,895
-Please, help yourselves, honored guests.
-Looks excellent.

164
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:20,565
-Who's there?
-I left late.

165
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:22,817
JEONG HYUN-GYU, 6TH ELIMINATED
OH HYUN-MIN, 8TH ELIMINATED

166
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,861
What's up, guys? How you been?

167
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:27,029
-Hyun-min.
-Congrats, girl. What was the challenge?

168
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:28,990
-Dude, I survived thanks to you.
-How did you do it?

169
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:31,909
-It was the 49. Forty-freakin'-nine.
-Oh, my God, no way.

170
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,203
But look, you succeeded. Look at you.

171
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:37,331
-Hyun-gyu, how goes?
-Can't complain.

172
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:39,167
-You've been through it.
-Feeling good?

173
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,918
Yeah. Congrats.

174
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,587
-Aw, thanks a bunch, man.
-Dude, wow.

175
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:45,298
-The prison!
-Hyun-min, we just missed each other.

176
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:48,342
-Bro, why did you leave so early?
-How's it going? Bring it in.

177
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:52,722
-Come on, now.
-Don't be like that, bud.

178
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:55,016
-Hey, get over there.
-Don't be shy, dude.

179
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:57,101
-Come on.
-He's reunited with his papa.

180
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,352
Oh, my gosh, he's crying.

181
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,937
-There, there, my son.
-Not again.

182
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,689
Give me a break.

183
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:03,524
We can't let him crumble like this.

184
00:08:03,608 --> 00:08:05,318
There, there. Aw…

185
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:07,528
You're making him cry even harder.

186
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,363
-Keep patting his back.
-Oh, I see.

187
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:11,240
Leave it to me, my boy.
I'll make you rich.

188
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,451
-I…
-You're the best.

189
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:14,994
Hey, all you students in Korea,

190
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,954
you should take classes from Hyun-min.

191
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,873
Hmm?

192
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:21,125
Learn from him and you'll be a genius too.

193
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,877
-You have to win.
-Don't you worry.

194
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,171
You gotta.

195
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,006
SHINDONG, 4TH ELIMINATED
HA SEOK-JIN, 7TH ELIMINATED

196
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:28,216
-What's up?
-Come on in.

197
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,760
-Oh, my good Lord.
-Get the hell over here.

198
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:32,637
-Hey!
-Hell yeah. Look at all of you.

199
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,597
-So good to see you guys.
-Who's in the finals?

200
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,642
-Hey, there, good to see you.
-Oh, my God this is great.

201
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,977
Oh, no hug for you.

202
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:42,522
-No way, get away from me.
-No, no, don't even bother.

203
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:44,065
I'll get to you.
Wait your turn over there.

204
00:08:44,148 --> 00:08:46,192
Just wait as far over there as possible.

205
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:47,693
-Did you make it?
-Good God.

206
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,278
Well, what can I say?

207
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,822
Dude, you have to stop winning.

208
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:53,574
-Ah, congrats, though.
-Sorry, man.

209
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:54,659
I'm in the final.

210
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,910
-Both of you guys?
-Yeah.

211
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:58,621
-Oh! Oh, this is gonna be good.
-Yeah.

212
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:01,082
-No, for real, how you feeling?
-Hey, man.

213
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:03,125
-I'm good. I… Yeah.
-Nice, nice, good to hear.

214
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:06,170
-Did you take the challenge?
-No, it was JAE JAE. She pulled it off.

215
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:07,672
-JAE JAE.
-Yeah?

216
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:09,215
How did you figure it out?

217
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:10,591
Yeah, right?

218
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:12,426
I spent the whole day
trying everything I could.

219
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:14,178
HONG JIN-HO, 2ND ELIMINATED
STELLA JANG, 5TH ELIMINATED

220
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:15,513
-Hey, guys! Oh!
-Who is it?

221
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:17,223
-No way!
-Oh, my God!

222
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:19,016
-Who made it to the final?
-Welcome back.

223
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,102
-Are you one of 'em?
-If it isn't Stella Jang, huh?

224
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,645
-Would you expect anything less?
-A finalist?

225
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,522
This esteemed linguist
deciphered everything…

226
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:27,775
-You're unbelievable.
-Hey, why did you leave so early?

227
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:29,694
I missed you the most, seriously.

228
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,196
-What's the deal?
-I left right after you.

229
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,031
-Really? Oh.
-SJang.

230
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,950
I've never heard of you
through the legends…

231
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,326
Did you make it to the final?

232
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,078
The legends of a great linguist
named Stella Jang.

233
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,330
-Ah.
-Wait, did you end up in the exile zone?

234
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:43,749
This esteemed linguist
deciphered everything before leaving,

235
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:47,712
-allowing future generations to live…
-Oh, so the first-ever ancestor was you.

236
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:50,840
If it weren't for her, no one would've
been able to leave the exile zone.

237
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:52,508
Yeah, a lot of good that did me.

238
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,719
I got nothing out of it myself.

239
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:56,220
-Oof.
-Ah, well.

240
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,763
YI DO, 1ST ELIMINATED
NUCKSAL, 3RD ELIMINATED

241
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,432
-Oh, wow!
-Good to see you.

242
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,809
-Hey, let's ask Nucksal to guess.
-Oh, no no.

243
00:10:01,892 --> 00:10:03,477
-Come on in.
-Were you on the show?

244
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:08,524
If any of you all can figure out
who the two finalists are…

245
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,151
-Mm-hmm.
-…then you can, uh…

246
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,736
-Two finalists, huh?
-…rejoin the competition.

247
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,195
Ooh, ooh.

248
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,405
-It ain't over yet.
-Ooh.

249
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:15,823
-I still have a chance?
-Sure.

250
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:17,575
Yeah, no, that's a pass from me.

251
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,704
See, now you're just trolling us.

252
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:23,289
-We know you're one of them.
-Oh, hey.

253
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:25,833
-Good to see you. How are you?
-I've been pretty well.

254
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:28,586
I say that, though at the same time,
it's been tough.

255
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:30,463
See, I've been totally in the dark.

256
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:32,673
I don't know
when everyone else got eliminated.

257
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,258
It was a whole lot that's happened.

258
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,426
Now, when you say "a lot"…

259
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:38,929
I know Jang Dong-min is one,
so is the other Jeong Hyun-gyu? Or you?

260
00:10:39,013 --> 00:10:40,306
-Take a guess.
-What?

261
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:41,641
Guess based on the outfits.

262
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,226
-Outfits? Wait, is that the giveaway?
-Yeah.

263
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:46,020
Looking at the outfits…

264
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:51,192
Hold on. Your outfit
totally screams "finalist."

265
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:52,485
-Yeah, it's me.
-Really?

266
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:54,236
-Are you messing with me?
-Me and Jang Dong-min. For real.

267
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,529
It's no lie.

268
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:56,739
Seriously?

269
00:10:57,823 --> 00:10:59,033
-You made it?
-Yeah.

270
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,744
-Unbelievable, right?
-You're kidding me.

271
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:04,121
-It's true.
-Oh, my God. Congratulations to you.

272
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,665
-Thanks.
-Congratulations. That's amazing.

273
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,459
Hey, well, of course it all started
on that first day with your, you know…

274
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:10,169
-You're serious? You're really serious?
-Well…

275
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:12,630
'Cause I was hoping
you were gonna make it this far.

276
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,548
-You mean that? Oh, thanks a lot.
-I really did.

277
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,676
I'm rooting for Hyun Kyung-lyul.

278
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:18,302
He's my favorite, for sure.

279
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:21,430
And selfishly, even though
it was only for the first day,

280
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:23,516
it's because we got to team up
with each other.

281
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:25,810
So I'm rooting for you, Hyun Kyung-lyul.

282
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,937
I think I missed you
most of all, Won-young.

283
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,064
-You guys were as thick as thieves.
-Yeah, well, he's…

284
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,441
-I mean, I can trust this guy, so…
-Sure.

285
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:35,194
Hey, well, I missed you guys the most
because of our first night.

286
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,238
Solving that puzzle together

287
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:39,448
was the most noteworthy thing
I did before leaving.

288
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:42,201
That was like my greatest achievement
of the whole show.

289
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:43,577
I'll never forget it.

290
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:47,289
Kyung-lyul's around the same age as me,
so I really hope he wins this.

291
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:50,000
And after this is over, hopefully
he and I can become real friends.

292
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:51,127
Go, Kyung-lyul.

293
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:53,713
I can't help but think
Jang Dong-min will win.

294
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:56,465
But the one I'm rooting for
is Hyun Kyung-lyul.

295
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,509
If he managed to flip the script here,

296
00:11:58,592 --> 00:12:01,262
it'd be a real watershed moment
in the history of survival shows,

297
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:03,180
so I really hope he takes the crown.

298
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:05,266
After you win, treat us to something nice.

299
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:06,350
Naturally.

300
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:09,061
I know you're used to making it to finals,

301
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,522
-but how are the nerves? You feel good?
-Like he gets nervous.

302
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:13,566
-When it comes to finals…
-Uh-huh.

303
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:15,443
…you get nervous no matter how many times.

304
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:18,279
Yeah, but even if he played solo,
he'd still have been the winner.

305
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:19,989
-Yeah.
-I know he would've.

306
00:12:20,781 --> 00:12:23,325
Dong-min is definitely
gonna come out on top.

307
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,787
This is like negative b plus or minus
the square root of b squared

308
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:29,457
minus four ac, all over two a.

309
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:32,334
The formula says he'll be the winner
of <i>The Devil's Plan </i>Season 3.

310
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:35,004
I'd kill to see that again,
when we were all, like…

311
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:37,339
"How does he do that so quickly?"

312
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,800
Seriously, I was blown away from day one.

313
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:43,053
Yeah, totally. Like when I got to see you
do that one game in prison,

314
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:45,431
I was like, "Whoa. He's bad at this."

315
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:48,017
Oh, what, me?

316
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,019
I was like, "Jin-ho, what are you doing?"

317
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:52,605
If I was playing against you,
I would've won.

318
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,899
Think I'd be an easy win, do ya?

319
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,400
Ooh.

320
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,819
<i>The final match will begin shortly.</i>

321
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:01,906
-Yeah. Let's go.
-Let's go.

322
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:05,117
<i>All guests,</i>
<i>please make your way to the living area.</i>

323
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,368
Wait, the living area?

324
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:08,496
-Oh, good. I finally get to see it.
-We love to see it.

325
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:10,581
-Hell yeah, I can finally go there.
-The Living Area.

326
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:12,875
-I get to see it.
-You never saw it, right?

327
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,335
-No, this'll be my first time.
-Let's go!

328
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:16,420
-I'm so excited.
-Living area!

329
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,714
I wanna see what it looks like.
Go, go, go, quickly.

330
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:20,925
-Root for me.
-Yeah, of course.

331
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:23,427
-Good luck.
-Thanks, man.

332
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,304
-I believe in you.
-Good luck.

333
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:27,014
-Thanks. Thank you.
-Lots of luck.

334
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:30,100
-One, two, three.
-Let's go!

335
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:32,102
It just felt right.

336
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:35,356
-Thanks.
-Good luck, dude.

337
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:36,607
Thank you, guys.

338
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,780
It's my first time seeing the living area.

339
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:43,906
Whoa!

340
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:45,574
Amazing!

341
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,493
Ooh, ooh!

342
00:13:47,576 --> 00:13:49,286
-Look, they have a gym!
-Whoa.

343
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,496
This place is crazy.

344
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:52,623
Seriously, the beds are all
just out in the open.

345
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:54,542
You guys can spy on each other out here.

346
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:57,336
Oh, down there was where
we could see you guys from below.

347
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:59,463
I made eye contact with Dong-jae.

348
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,966
Oh, crap, I think he spotted me.

349
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,801
Damn, you can see
the whole prison from up here.

350
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:05,636
I could see your backs
when you were sitting here.

351
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,555
You know, up close, it's not all that.

352
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:10,057
Yeah, it really isn't.
It's really not that special.

353
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:12,017
Always wondered
what the living area looks like.

354
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:14,144
-First time laying eyes on it.
-Go right, go right.

355
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:15,855
-Oh, wait.
-That's the prison.

356
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,022
My feet were lying to me.

357
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:19,984
It's in your blood now, man.
You're a prisoner for life.

358
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,945
-For life?
-It was magnetizing me.

359
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:25,781
-Yo, this is nice.
-Wow.

360
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,951
-There's the prison down there.
-Man, it's like a swanky hotel.

361
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:30,619
Wow.

362
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,246
Tell me they got coffee in here.

363
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:34,832
Coffee right here, dude.
Got a machine and KANU.

364
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:37,960
-Nice, I need me a cup of that.
-I'm gonna have a yukgaejang.

365
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,005
Right, because we've been
so starved of food.

366
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,089
-Yeah.
-Ice?

367
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:43,799
Oh, they actually have yukgaejang.

368
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:47,511
This place is so open.
It's a lot like the exile zone.

369
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:48,929
-Uh…
-You're talking crazy.

370
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:51,056
-It's not nearly as terrifying.
-It's pretty similar.

371
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,683
-Can't make that comparison.
-Not even close.

372
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,518
Not to mention, the exile zone was also--

373
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,270
The exile zone was practically outdoors.

374
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:59,273
The ceiling in here is so high,
it's almost like being outdoors.

375
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:03,569
Well, as the first ever
official archaeologist of the exile zone,

376
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:07,990
I've written this kind of
puzzle-slash-letter thing

377
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:11,577
in loving memory of the massive headache
that place gave me.

378
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,871
It looks like this.

379
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:16,582
Um… "Life is death."

380
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:19,668
"Living a day is the same as dying a day."

381
00:15:20,878 --> 00:15:25,174
"I did not know how to see things
through the mind of God."

382
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:29,261
"I am dead, but I am happy
to have been able to compete."

383
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:34,391
"When the night ends and the sun rises,

384
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:37,394
we will know who the final winner is."

385
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:40,147
The vocab in the exile zone
is pretty limited,

386
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:43,567
so I had to make up some words
that didn't exist in their lexicon.

387
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,027
-This is it, huh?
-What?

388
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:46,362
This is the whole living area?

389
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:48,697
-Park, you never made it up here?
-Nothing special.

390
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:50,449
-He's the longest survivor.
-King of the prison.

391
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,785
-So you spent this whole show in prison?
-Yeah.

392
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:55,371
-That's rough, buddy.
-No, he didn't even wanna be up here.

393
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:57,665
He was throwing the matches
on purpose, like,

394
00:15:57,748 --> 00:15:59,667
"No, I can't go to the living area."

395
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:05,130
If I had to guess, you two are probably
both rooting for Dong-min?

396
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:06,423
Goes without saying.

397
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:09,468
-I guess I should if I'm--
-Well, assuming there's no major upsets.

398
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:12,846
But if Kyung-lyul wins, that'd make
the final match a lot more interesting,

399
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,307
-so I hope he does well.
-Me too. For once, I'd like the underdog

400
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:17,142
-to get his moment in the sun.
-Yeah, agreed.

401
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:19,269
No, I'm eating my yukgaejang.

402
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:20,562
This is how we watch it?

403
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,606
-You can eat and watch, come on.
-Is this okay?

404
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:26,443
This side's more relaxing.
Kind of nice being a spectator.

405
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:29,029
-Oh, my God, there they are.
-It's time.

406
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:52,011
-They look awesome.
-Hell yeah, they do.

407
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:05,733
<i>Greetings, finalists.</i>

408
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:07,776
<i>Congratulations to both of you</i>

409
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:10,571
<i>on making it to the finale</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan.

410
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:16,326
<i>Yesterday, JAE JAE and John Park</i>
<i>were eliminated in the prison match,</i>

411
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:19,913
<i>leaving you, Jang Dong-min</i>
<i>and Hyun Kyung-lyul,</i>

412
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,498
<i>as our two finalists.</i>

413
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:26,045
<i>The prize money accumulated so far</i>
<i>through the prize tokens</i>

414
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:27,963
<i>is 200 million won.</i>

415
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,716
This is from that hidden thing
Won-young did?

416
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,720
<i>Now, I shall present to you</i>
<i>the games of the final.</i>

417
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:38,557
<i>The final match</i>
<i>will consist of three games.</i>

418
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:42,519
<i>The first of the final games</i>
<i>is Card Janggi.</i>

419
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:44,813
<i>This abstract strategy game</i>

420
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:47,983
<i>requires decisive judgment</i>
<i>to read your opponent's moves.</i>

421
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,027
Isn't Janggi Dong-min's wheelhouse?

422
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,154
-Yeah, he's really good at Janggi.
-Right?

423
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:54,615
<i>The second game is Color Link.</i>

424
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:59,536
<i>This is a strategy game that requires</i>
<i>both expert spatial perception,</i>

425
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,538
<i>as well as problem-solving skills.</i>

426
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:05,250
<i>And the third and final game</i>
<i>is Equation Traffic Light.</i>

427
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:08,879
<i>This game requires logical reasoning</i>
<i>and arithmetic skills.</i>

428
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:10,380
I freaking hate that game.

429
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:15,302
<i>The player who wins</i>
<i>two out of three games first</i>

430
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:16,720
<i>will be the final winner</i>

431
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:20,349
<i>and take home the prize money</i>
<i>of 200 million won.</i>

432
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:22,559
<i>Now, we will begin the final match</i>

433
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:25,813
<i>to determine the winner</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan.

434
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,153
Hey there.

435
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:39,868
<i>I will now walk you through</i>
<i>the rules of the first game of the final.</i>

436
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:47,167
<i>To refresh, the first</i>
<i>of the three games is Card Janggi.</i>

437
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:48,710
<i>In Card Janggi,</i>

438
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:51,421
<i>you decide the order</i>
<i>of your five movement cards</i>

439
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:54,174
<i>and either land</i>
<i>on your opponent's great piece square</i>

440
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:56,802
<i>or capture their great piece</i>
<i>to win the game.</i>

441
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:00,806
<i>Each player will start</i>
<i>with one great piece,</i>

442
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:04,518
<i>three small pieces,</i>
<i>and five movement cards.</i>

443
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:08,814
<i>Each piece begins</i>
<i>in a fixed starting position.</i>

444
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:13,527
<i>And each movement card</i>
<i>shows a different type of move.</i>

445
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:17,614
<i>The animal motif indicates</i>
<i>the piece's current position,</i>

446
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:21,451
<i>and the gray squares show</i>
<i>where it can move when that card is used.</i>

447
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:26,790
<i>The player to make the first move</i>
<i>will be decided by a coin toss,</i>

448
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:30,210
<i>after which, you will take turns</i>
<i>being the first player.</i>

449
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,213
<i>The player with the first move</i>
<i>will need to use</i>

450
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,215
<i>all five of their movement cards,</i>

451
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:38,886
<i>while the second player will only</i>
<i>need to use four out of their five.</i>

452
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:41,680
<i>Once the first player is decided,</i>

453
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:44,433
<i>both of you arrange</i>
<i>the order of your movement cards</i>

454
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:46,560
<i>and place them face down.</i>

455
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:49,146
-Right away?
-Ah, gotta do it from the start.

456
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:50,522
<i>Once the cards have been set,</i>

457
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:54,776
<i>both players will reveal</i>
<i>their first movement card simultaneously.</i>

458
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:58,697
<i>Then, they will move their pieces</i>
<i>according to the order of your cards.</i>

459
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:01,408
<i>Starting with the first player,</i>

460
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:04,244
<i>each of you will have</i>
<i>a maximum of 90 seconds</i>

461
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:07,789
<i>to move one of your pieces</i>
<i>according to your first card.</i>

462
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:11,460
<i>After you make your move,</i>
<i>you will flip over your next card.</i>

463
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:13,503
Oh, we have to.

464
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,672
<i>When one of your pieces lands on a square</i>

465
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:17,841
<i>occupied by an opponent's piece,</i>

466
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:20,510
<i>that piece will be removed from the board.</i>

467
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:25,974
<i>Next, after the second player</i>
<i>uses their last movement card,</i>

468
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:29,728
<i>they must immediately</i>
<i>rearrange all five of their cards,</i>

469
00:20:29,811 --> 00:20:32,940
<i>leaving the first card face up.</i>

470
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:34,816
Hmm, they go back and forth.

471
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,401
<i>The first player will then be allowed</i>

472
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:39,154
<i>to look at the second player's</i>
<i>first movement card</i>

473
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,907
<i>before using the last of their own cards.</i>

474
00:20:41,990 --> 00:20:46,245
<i>After that, the first player will</i>
<i>need to rearrange their cards as well,</i>

475
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:48,664
<i>leaving the first one face up.</i>

476
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:50,999
<i>And then, from that point on,</i>

477
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,961
<i>both players use all five cards.</i>

478
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:56,588
<i>The game shall continue in this manner</i>

479
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:59,758
<i>until one of two scenarios play out.</i>

480
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:03,553
<i>A: A player's great piece</i>
<i>lands on the starting square</i>

481
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:05,931
<i>of their opponent's great piece.</i>

482
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:10,310
<i>Or B: If a player captures</i>
<i>their opponent's great piece.</i>

483
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,562
<i>Either option will end the game.</i>

484
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:15,607
<i>If you fail to move</i>
<i>within the 90-second time limit,</i>

485
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:19,152
<i>your opponent gets to move your piece</i>
<i>wherever they want</i>

486
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:21,530
<i>according to the card currently in play.</i>

487
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,907
<i>Think fast and do not forget this penalty.</i>

488
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:29,246
<i>Finally, this match</i>
<i>will be best out of three rounds.</i>

489
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:31,999
<i>The first player to win two rounds</i>
<i>will be the winner.</i>

490
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,084
<i>Before we begin the game,</i>

491
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:37,587
<i>both of you will be allowed to choose</i>
<i>one player from the living area</i>

492
