His king's invincible.

674
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:31,412
-Yeah, it's over.
-Right?

675
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:34,415
I've realized I've lost.

676
00:30:42,924 --> 00:30:45,009
-Yo, I think that was the elephant.
-Huh?

677
00:30:45,093 --> 00:30:46,594
What? Is it actually?

678
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:49,055
He just needs a cross pattern
in the first slot.

679
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:51,975
Please turn over your first card.

680
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:04,195
This was my chance to win
right out the gate,

681
00:31:05,822 --> 00:31:07,198
and I immediately blew it.

682
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:10,201
When you make a blunder
at as critical a moment as that,

683
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:13,204
staying cool-headed feels impossible.

684
00:31:13,288 --> 00:31:16,457
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please make your move.

685
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:23,882
Hyun Kyung-lyul,
please rearrange your cards.

686
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:29,554
I've got Dong-min's
great piece right in the crosshairs.

687
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:33,683
On this turn, as long as I lead
with the rat or the monkey,

688
00:31:33,766 --> 00:31:37,186
I can limit where Dong-min's great piece
can move to.

689
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:39,272
So now I'm making sure to arrange my cards

690
00:31:39,355 --> 00:31:42,483
with the goal of capturing
his great piece.

691
00:31:43,443 --> 00:31:45,278
Please turn over your first card.

692
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:49,365
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please make your move.

693
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:54,829
Please turn over your next card.

694
00:31:56,915 --> 00:31:58,249
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.

695
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:10,261
Please turn over your next card.

696
00:32:11,220 --> 00:32:12,764
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.

697
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:20,855
Please turn over your next card.

698
00:32:25,234 --> 00:32:26,945
I've decided my best strategy

699
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:29,322
is to move my king onto his king square.

700
00:32:29,405 --> 00:32:31,866
Okay, so one of the combos
I've come up with is

701
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:34,702
this, this and this,

702
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:36,579
-using three cards in a row.
-Mm-hmm.

703
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:39,582
And you land on that square like this,
or this, one of the two.

704
00:32:39,666 --> 00:32:42,043
In games like Janggi,
there's a lot of tactics

705
00:32:42,126 --> 00:32:44,587
where you can throw out
some tempting bait for your opponent,

706
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,215
and then you swoop in for the kill,
and that's what I like.

707
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:49,676
So I leave this one open, hmm?

708
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:51,803
And then he'll totally try
to go for the capture.

709
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:53,805
-Right.
-If I sacrifice that piece

710
00:32:53,888 --> 00:32:56,599
and follow up with a three-card combo,
he won't be able to stop it.

711
00:32:56,683 --> 00:33:00,812
Then, when my opponent
captures the piece in front of my king,

712
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,898
my king uses the elephant
to escape the zone,

713
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:05,900
then the giraffe to jump,

714
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,361
and finally,
the horse to land on the square,

715
00:33:08,444 --> 00:33:10,279
-and that's a three-turn kill.
-Nice.

716
00:33:10,905 --> 00:33:13,616
-So that's his strategy.
-Elephant, giraffe and horse for the win.

717
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,576
So the rat was the problem.

718
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,370
-It was just a throwaway move.
-Right.

719
00:33:20,581 --> 00:33:22,250
How the hell did I miss that?

720
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:27,213
Okay, I resign from this one.

721
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:30,508
Jang Dong-min wins round one.

722
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:32,427
Nice. Incredibly well played.

723
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:35,388
This game is tough.

724
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,432
Yeah, I screwed up.

725
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:39,976
I should've been looking at where
his pieces were heading into my zone,

726
00:33:40,059 --> 00:33:42,437
but I was only looking at
where my pieces were going.

727
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:43,938
Should've put more thought into it.

728
00:33:44,564 --> 00:33:46,607
We will now begin round two.

729
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:50,653
Jang Dong-min will move first,
Hyun Kyung-lyul will move second.

730
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:52,864
You have three minutes
to arrange your cards.

731
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:02,123
Initially, I was arranging my cards

732
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:04,208
just like Dong-min had done last round,

733
00:34:04,292 --> 00:34:05,918
mainly focusing on defense.

734
00:34:08,504 --> 00:34:11,591
RAT, MONKEY…

735
00:34:11,674 --> 00:34:14,010
But since Dong-min
already knows that arrangement

736
00:34:14,093 --> 00:34:15,344
like the back of his hand,

737
00:34:15,428 --> 00:34:17,930
he's probably already got
a different one to counter it.

738
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:21,350
So my new plan is,
if he plays defensively,

739
00:34:21,434 --> 00:34:23,978
I'm gonna slowly inch forward
two of my pieces.

740
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:27,065
And while he's defending,
I'll charge forward with my king,

741
00:34:27,148 --> 00:34:28,733
and see how he likes that.

742
00:34:28,816 --> 00:34:30,568
You have one minute left.

743
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:36,991
This round,
if an opportunity comes knocking,

744
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,159
I'm gonna attack.

745
00:34:38,242 --> 00:34:40,953
But otherwise, I'm waiting for him
to advance first.

746
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:44,123
And whatever he tries to do,
I'll be ready for it.

747
00:34:45,333 --> 00:34:46,667
Ten seconds remain.

748
00:34:51,380 --> 00:34:53,091
-It's round two.
-Here we go again.

749
00:34:53,174 --> 00:34:55,510
-Come on, Kyung-lyul. Win this.
-He'll do it.

750
00:34:55,593 --> 00:34:57,261
Let's see how this goes.

751
00:34:57,970 --> 00:34:59,764
Please turn over your first card.

752
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:05,812
Wait a minute. What's this?

753
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:08,231
Kyung-lyul's coming out
with guns a-blazing.

754
00:35:08,314 --> 00:35:10,566
The elephant can't do much
on your first move.

755
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:11,776
What is he thinking?

756
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:14,153
Jang Dong-min, please make your move.

757
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:22,995
Please turn over your next card.

758
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:26,541
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.

759
00:35:26,624 --> 00:35:28,084
Interesting second card.

760
00:35:28,167 --> 00:35:30,169
Yeah, but no matter what he placed,

761
00:35:30,253 --> 00:35:32,171
he'd still be able
to defend against anything.

762
00:35:32,255 --> 00:35:33,589
Now he's untouchable.

763
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:36,259
There's no better
starting setup than that.

764
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:46,477
One minute remains.

765
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,402
He's sending out the king.

766
00:35:54,485 --> 00:35:56,863
-Look at him, he's just going for it.
-Yep.

767
00:35:56,946 --> 00:35:59,699
He could get in there right
away with a giraffe and then a horse.

768
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:01,826
-Oh, yeah.
-Elephant, giraffe, horse.

769
00:36:02,535 --> 00:36:04,245
Please turn over your next card.

770
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:06,706
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.

771
00:36:21,804 --> 00:36:24,182
Whoa. Depending on
what Dong-min's third card is,

772
00:36:24,265 --> 00:36:26,184
this round could be over immediately.

773
00:36:26,267 --> 00:36:27,977
-Yeah, like, in a blink.
-Yep.

774
00:36:28,060 --> 00:36:29,979
-He's got nowhere to go.
-Good Lord…

775
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:32,398
Please turn over your next card.

776
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,318
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.

777
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:37,528
Aw, shit.

778
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:43,075
Now Kyung-lyul's king has nowhere to go.

779
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:44,785
Had a feeling he'd think twice.

780
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:47,455
He got cold feet
about repeating the same process,

781
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:49,498
leading with the rat or the monkey.

782
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:52,001
So now he's gonna have to come up
with something better

783
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:55,171
if he wants any shot at rattling
Jang Dong-min.

784
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:57,131
His king is cornered.

785
00:36:57,215 --> 00:36:59,091
His own pawns are blocking
his one escape route.

786
00:36:59,175 --> 00:37:01,594
-Yeah, it's all blocked.
-Kyung-lyul might be cooked.

787
00:37:03,888 --> 00:37:06,515
I didn't expect
any of his cards to be what he picked,

788
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:09,769
and now I'm so messed up, I can't
calculate anything properly anymore.

789
00:37:09,852 --> 00:37:13,564
None of my strategies are working,
and I'm making too many crappy moves.

790
00:37:18,277 --> 00:37:20,196
Please turn over your next card.

791
00:37:21,405 --> 00:37:23,241
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.

792
00:37:28,287 --> 00:37:31,874
Jang Dong-min has captured
Hyun Kyung-lyul's great piece,

793
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:34,168
making him the winner of round two.

794
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:36,837
Too bad. This one's a bummer.

795
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:39,298
That first round shook him to his core.

796
00:37:39,382 --> 00:37:42,301
The final match is nerve-racking.
You're gonna make mistakes.

797
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:47,265
<i>Jang Dong-min, you have won</i>
<i>the first game of the final match, 2-0.</i>

798
00:37:47,348 --> 00:37:50,810
<i>The second game of the final</i>
<i>will begin shortly.</i>

799
00:37:53,396 --> 00:37:54,730
Okay. Bring on the next one.

800
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:56,399
So if he wins the second game,

801
00:37:56,482 --> 00:38:00,111
he'll be taking the competition
with a 100% win rate, yeah?

802
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:01,904
-Without a single loss?
-Wow.

803
00:38:01,988 --> 00:38:04,115
Ah, this hurts.

804
00:38:09,537 --> 00:38:11,747
No, don't even worry about it.
You got this.

805
00:38:12,957 --> 00:38:16,127
<i>With that, I shall now</i>
<i>walk you through the second game.</i>

806
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:20,256
<i>The next game of the final match</i>
<i>is Color Link.</i>

807
00:38:21,549 --> 00:38:23,968
<i>In Color Link, you must place pieces</i>

808
00:38:24,051 --> 00:38:27,722
<i>so that the paths connecting</i>
<i>all of your pieces of the same color</i>

809
00:38:27,805 --> 00:38:29,265
<i>do not overlap.</i>

810
00:38:30,766 --> 00:38:33,519
<i>The game uses a total of 28 pieces,</i>

811
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:36,397
<i>comprised of 14 pairs of different colors.</i>

812
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,900
That many? All the way up to N?

813
00:38:39,984 --> 00:38:41,444
<i>Before the game starts,</i>

814
00:38:41,527 --> 00:38:44,488
<i>the first player will be decided</i>
<i>by a coin toss.</i>

815
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:47,116
<i>Then, from the second round onward,</i>

816
00:38:47,199 --> 00:38:50,745
<i>the loser of the previous round</i>
<i>decides who will be the first player.</i>

817
00:38:50,828 --> 00:38:51,829
They get to choose?

818
00:38:51,912 --> 00:38:53,372
<i>Once the board is revealed,</i>

819
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:56,417
<i>the player who goes first</i>
<i>must place one piece.</i>

820
00:38:57,293 --> 00:38:59,503
<i>Thereafter, you will both take turns</i>

821
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:03,591
<i>placing two pieces of different colors</i>
<i>within a three-minute time limit.</i>

822
00:39:04,592 --> 00:39:08,637
<i>Act fast, for if you fail to place</i>
<i>the pieces before time is up,</i>

823
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:11,057
<i>you will immediately lose the round.</i>

824
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:12,767
Oh…

825
00:39:12,850 --> 00:39:13,851
<i>And take note:</i>

826
00:39:13,934 --> 00:39:16,312
<i>The pieces must be placed such</i>

827
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:19,607
<i>that if every pair on the board</i>
<i>were connected,</i>

828
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:22,860
<i>none of the paths would overlap</i>
<i>or intersect.</i>

829
00:39:22,943 --> 00:39:25,613
<i>Even if only one of a pair</i>
<i>is on the board,</i>

830
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:28,824
<i>it must still be possible</i>
<i>to connect it to its matching piece</i>

831
00:39:28,908 --> 00:39:30,910
<i>without violating the rules.</i>

832
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:34,955
<i>In addition, the path connecting</i>
<i>each pair of same-colored pieces</i>

833
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:37,249
<i>must be at least six squares long,</i>

834
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:40,503
<i>including the squares</i>
<i>the pieces themselves occupy.</i>

835
00:39:41,087 --> 00:39:42,922
<i>If, after your opponent's turn,</i>

836
00:39:43,005 --> 00:39:45,674
<i>you believe that the paths</i>
<i>connecting the pairs on the board</i>

837
00:39:45,758 --> 00:39:47,510
<i>overlap or intersect,</i>

838
00:39:47,593 --> 00:39:51,347
<i>then as an alternative move,</i>
<i>you may declare impossibility.</i>

839
00:39:51,972 --> 00:39:53,641
So like calling out your opponent.

840
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,810
<i>When impossibility is declared,</i>

841
00:39:55,893 --> 00:39:59,438
<i>the player who just played their turn</i>
<i>has five minutes to prove</i>

842
00:39:59,522 --> 00:40:02,983
<i>that all of the same-colored pairs</i>
<i>on the board can be connected</i>

843
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:05,778
<i>without any overlaps or intersections.</i>

844
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:08,906
<i>If only one of a pair is on the board,</i>

845
00:40:08,989 --> 00:40:11,784
<i>the player must place the matching piece</i>

846
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:14,703
<i>and prove that this pair</i>
<i>can also be connected</i>

847
00:40:14,787 --> 00:40:17,206
<i>according to the rules we've explained.</i>

848
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:19,250
Ah.

849
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:20,835
Oh, that's tough.

850
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:24,713
<i>If that player could then</i>
<i>successfully prove all of the connections,</i>

851
00:40:24,797 --> 00:40:26,507
<i>they will earn one point.</i>

852
00:40:27,508 --> 00:40:30,845
<i>However, if they fail</i>
<i>to prove their arrangements,</i>

853
00:40:30,928 --> 00:40:35,516
<i>the player who declared impossibility</i>
<i>will earn one piece instead.</i>

854
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,310
<i>This game will consist</i>
<i>of five rounds in total,</i>

855
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:41,856
<i>and the first player to earn three points</i>
<i>will be declared the winner.</i>

856
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:46,986
<i>That is all. The second game</i>
<i>of the final match will begin shortly.</i>

857
00:40:49,738 --> 00:40:52,158
-Looks like a different board each time.
-I see, the board's gonna change.

858
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:55,035
-It being different each round is rough.
-"A new board is revealed."

859
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:59,540
-If there are 14 colors and 28 pieces…
-Then it wouldn't work.

860
00:40:59,623 --> 00:41:01,125
-It couldn't be small.
-Ten…

861
00:41:01,208 --> 00:41:03,461
The mappings are probably
gonna look ridiculous.

862
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:05,629
There's no way there won't be
intersecting paths,

863
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:06,964
even with a big board.

864
00:41:07,047 --> 00:41:09,175
Let's look at a seven-by-seven board.

865
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:13,554
I swear, Won-young, you're never tired.

866
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:15,097
-Anybody?
-Yep.

867
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,099
How did he get eliminated?

868
00:41:17,183 --> 00:41:19,185
He somehow got through the exile zone

869
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:22,646
and advanced to the semifinal
as the last man standing.

870
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:26,400
The main match was a betting game,
and he went all in on his very first hand.

871
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:30,154
-And crashed out?
-All in, but Jang Dong-min took him out.

872
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:31,864
Brutal.

873
00:41:31,947 --> 00:41:34,408
-Why would you do that to yourself?
-Something got him confident.

874
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,327
-It wasn't right off the bat.
-That's conviction.

875
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:38,996
I was only gonna bet three chips
and take the pot,

876
00:41:39,079 --> 00:41:41,999
but Dong-min already had
a made hand right off the deal.

877
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:44,585
You betrayed me just to fail?

878
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:48,172
-Sorry, bud.
-Killed me off only to go and blow it?

879
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:50,799
Well, maybe you should've opened the door
and taken on the curse.

880
00:41:51,967 --> 00:41:53,427
So they come in pairs, huh?

881
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:55,930
-Let's do this.
-Let's.

882
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:03,062
A game of impossibilities and proof.

883
00:42:03,145 --> 00:42:05,105
Suppose I could say

884
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:09,068
those are the words that made me
the Jang Dong-min that I am today.

885
00:42:09,151 --> 00:42:10,861
Will I be proving myself,

886
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:14,073
or will I be the man
who makes the impossible possible?

887
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:16,325
Either scenario feels like fate.

888
00:42:16,408 --> 00:42:17,576
Or maybe destiny.

889
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:21,413
People in my field of work have algorithms

890
00:42:21,497 --> 00:42:22,873
to figure out things like this.

891
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:25,084
If there's one battle I shouldn't lose,
it's this one.

892
00:42:25,167 --> 00:42:28,712
If I win Color Link, the final game
will be Equation Traffic Light.

893
00:42:29,463 --> 00:42:31,882
And when it comes
to both this game and the next one,

894
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:35,010
I'm confident that I'm just as good
as Jang Dong-min.

895
00:42:35,094 --> 00:42:36,762
No, better than him, even.

896
00:42:36,845 --> 00:42:39,765
So I'm determined to even the score
by winning Color Link

897
00:42:39,848 --> 00:42:41,642
and stage a dramatic comeback.

898
00:42:42,309 --> 00:42:46,146
<i>The current score is 1-0</i>
<i>in favor of Jang Dong-min.</i>

899
00:42:47,231 --> 00:42:49,900
<i>If Jang Dong-min is victorious</i>
<i>in this game,</i>

900
00:42:49,984 --> 00:42:53,988
<i>he will be declared</i>
<i>the final winner of </i>The Devil's Plan.

901
00:42:57,449 --> 00:43:00,119
