gonna get all tangled up.

923
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:28,123
Oh!

924
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:30,125
-A wraparound?
-He's trapping the Y's.

925
00:44:30,209 --> 00:44:32,211
-I think he's circling the entire board.
-I see it now.

926
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,296
The whole outer line is nulled out.

927
00:44:34,380 --> 00:44:36,340
So they have to go all the way around.

928
00:44:36,423 --> 00:44:37,716
He basically just shrunk the board.

929
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:39,385
Absolutely what he was going for.

930
00:44:45,933 --> 00:44:49,186
I put the B there to reduce
the number of paths for the Y's.

931
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:52,773
In my head, I've already mapped out
the paths for the Y's and the X's,

932
00:44:52,856 --> 00:44:55,359
and I've also mapped out
the path for the B's too.

933
00:44:55,442 --> 00:44:57,403
I don't know where the other B will go,

934
00:44:57,486 --> 00:44:59,279
but it can't be placed near the existing B

935
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:00,989
unless there's a six-square space.

936
00:45:01,073 --> 00:45:04,034
So reducing the number of possibilities
will be to my advantage.

937
00:45:04,118 --> 00:45:06,412
And I got a clear idea
where the paths will go,

938
00:45:06,495 --> 00:45:09,331
but Dong-min will probably
welcome the challenge.

939
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:12,209
-He might still have a chance.
-Yeah, he totally does.

940
00:45:12,292 --> 00:45:13,627
I think he's gonna do good on this.

941
00:45:13,711 --> 00:45:16,755
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

942
00:45:28,976 --> 00:45:30,269
Thirty seconds remain.

943
00:45:32,354 --> 00:45:35,023
Guess their strategy is to cut off
the previous player's move

944
00:45:35,107 --> 00:45:36,108
before placing a new pair.

945
00:45:36,191 --> 00:45:38,152
Might be the only thing
they feel they can do.

946
00:45:38,235 --> 00:45:40,529
If that's the case,
then, really, this is a battle

947
00:45:40,612 --> 00:45:42,698
