-We'll see if he's right.

968
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:04,506
Jang Dong-min, you have
five minutes to prove the connections.

969
00:48:06,842 --> 00:48:09,595
You must place the matching piece
for the unpaired one

970
00:48:09,678 --> 00:48:11,138
before you complete your proof.

971
00:48:11,889 --> 00:48:13,557
Assuming I can draw on the board?

972
00:48:13,640 --> 00:48:15,309
Prove the connections using the marker.

973
00:48:26,028 --> 00:48:27,529
-A downward X path.
-Maybe it does work?

974
00:48:27,613 --> 00:48:29,406
He'd have to draw the same
for the Y's too.

975
00:48:29,489 --> 00:48:31,617
-That's gonna be harder.
-But he can't do that.

976
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:33,452
No, the Cs won't connect then.

977
00:48:33,535 --> 00:48:35,787
-He's right. There's not enough room.
-Same thing with the two D's.

978
00:48:35,871 --> 00:48:37,247
D can use six squares,

979
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:39,666
-but C's only got five.
-Oh…

980
00:49:07,194 --> 00:49:08,570
One minute remains.

981
00:49:12,199 --> 00:49:14,910
-Ooh, he looks cool standing like that.
-Right?

982
00:49:14,993 --> 00:49:17,204
-Whoa.
-Confident little head shake.

983
00:49:20,707 --> 00:49:23,043
Hey, he might've pulled it off.

984
00:49:23,126 --> 00:49:24,962
Oh, so awesome.

985
00:49:25,587 --> 00:49:27,381
This is a game no computer science

986
00:49:27,464 --> 00:49:29,257
or algorithm expert could ever lose.

987
00:49:29,841 --> 00:49:31,551
By placing the C and the D where I did,

988
00:49:31,635 --> 00:49:34,137
I made it impossible
for any other letters to connect.

989
00:49:34,721 --> 00:49:37,516
So when I was picking
where C and D would sit,

990
00:49:37,599 --> 00:49:39,768
I was already planning
to declare impossibility,

991
00:49:39,851 --> 00:49:42,229
