995
00:49:50,278 --> 00:49:52,364
-Oh, you're right.
-He, like, shrunk the whole board.

996
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:54,157
Ten seconds remain.

997
00:49:56,743 --> 00:50:01,415
Five, four, three, two, one.

998
00:50:02,290 --> 00:50:03,625
Your time has run out.

999
00:50:04,334 --> 00:50:07,170
<i>Jang Dong-min has failed</i>
<i>to prove the connections.</i>

1000
00:50:07,254 --> 00:50:10,215
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul has earned himself</i>
<i>one point.</i>

1001
00:50:11,133 --> 00:50:13,844
Wow. I feel like
I'm watching an action flick.

1002
00:50:13,927 --> 00:50:16,430
-Nice job.
-Not a total loss yet.

1003
00:50:16,513 --> 00:50:18,682
He might actually take this one.
He could win Color Link.

1004
00:50:18,765 --> 00:50:20,475
Anything could happen
when the momentum shifts.

1005
00:50:20,559 --> 00:50:22,144
-Yeah.
-I get what you mean by that.

1006
00:50:22,227 --> 00:50:24,813
Now I'm confident, at least in this game,

1007
00:50:24,896 --> 00:50:26,648
I could beat even Dong-min.

1008
00:50:26,732 --> 00:50:28,817
Well, you should
always leave your opponent

1009
00:50:28,900 --> 00:50:30,402
with only one possible option,

1010
00:50:30,485 --> 00:50:32,029
and this time I…

1011
00:50:34,364 --> 00:50:36,074
We'll move to the next round.

1012
00:50:36,825 --> 00:50:38,994
Here is the board for round two.

1013
00:50:42,289 --> 00:50:43,790
-Yeah!
-Good God.

1014
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:45,625
That's what I'm talking about.

1015
00:50:45,709 --> 00:50:47,252
How the hell do you do this one?

1016
00:50:47,335 --> 00:50:48,879
Oh, I can tell.

1017
00:50:48,962 --> 00:50:51,214
You gotta force a violation
on your opponent.

1018
00:50:51,298 --> 00:50:55,302
Jang Dong-min, you have three minutes
to choose between going first or second.

1019
00:51:02,809 --> 00:51:05,395
Man, even choosing
the turn order's super critical.

1020
00:51:08,690 --> 00:51:11,193
-I'll go second.
-You have chosen to go second.

1021
00:51:11,276 --> 00:51:13,904
Then, Hyun Kyung-lyul,
you'll be the first player.

1022
00:51:13,987 --> 00:51:16,865
You have three minutes
to place your first piece.

1023
00:51:24,748 --> 00:51:28,085
If I were playing, I'd just put
the first piece smack dab in the middle.

1024
00:51:28,168 --> 00:51:31,088
Like, just block off the entrance
and reduce any movements.

1025
00:51:31,171 --> 00:51:34,424
I'd put the first one in the middle
and then another one on the outside.

1026
00:51:34,508 --> 00:51:36,760
-Clog up the whole tract for everybody.
-That'd be insane.

1027
00:51:36,843 --> 00:51:39,137
-One player gets to make the opening move.
-For this round?

1028
00:51:39,221 --> 00:51:42,140
-One piece will decide everything.
-Mmm. But that single piece?

1029
00:51:42,224 --> 00:51:44,101
There's a million wrong moves
you could make.

1030
00:51:44,184 --> 00:51:47,145
I couldn't tell you
the most strategic place to put it.

1031
00:51:48,855 --> 00:51:52,025
Dong-min must have a damn
good reason for choosing to go second,

1032
00:51:52,109 --> 00:51:54,319
maybe based on the number
of squares or something.

1033
00:52:00,117 --> 00:52:03,787
So I choose to put it there, hoping
it might throw off his calculations.

1034
00:52:05,288 --> 00:52:08,542
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1035
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:28,103
Whoa, that's a move.

1036
00:52:28,186 --> 00:52:29,729
A B and a C, interesting.

1037
00:52:29,813 --> 00:52:31,481
With those two letters in those spaces?

1038
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:34,860
Now, no more than a pair each
can fit on the left and right sides.

1039
00:52:35,485 --> 00:52:38,446
I think Dong-min's already
mapped everything out in his head.

1040
00:52:38,530 --> 00:52:41,032
After the first round, I was thinking

1041
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:42,909
about this odd-number strategy,

1042
00:52:42,993 --> 00:52:46,246
where, basically, you figure out
in advance the total number of pairs

1043
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:48,623
that can be connected
on that particular board,

1044
00:52:48,707 --> 00:52:52,669
and pass the turn to your opponent
with an odd number of unpaired pieces,

1045
00:52:52,752 --> 00:52:55,505
whatever they may be,
while ensuring that on your own turn,

1046
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:56,798
all the connections work.

1047
00:52:57,382 --> 00:52:59,092
And you'll never be put at a disadvantage.

1048
00:52:59,176 --> 00:53:01,761
And so, that strategy gave me the idea

1049
00:53:01,845 --> 00:53:04,598
to place a B and a C
on either side of the A,

1050
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:08,268
cutting off all possible paths
for A right from the get-go.

1051
00:53:08,351 --> 00:53:11,313
Other than, obviously,
the one path that goes upwards.

1052
00:53:11,396 --> 00:53:15,150
And now, I can control how many pieces
can still be placed on the board.

1053
00:53:15,233 --> 00:53:18,236
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1054
00:53:21,531 --> 00:53:23,617
The way Dong-min laid down the B and C,

1055
00:53:23,700 --> 00:53:26,536
there's two paths that can be created
on the board, maybe more.

1056
00:53:26,620 --> 00:53:29,164
So I'm still trying to reduce
the number of possible paths.

1057
00:53:29,247 --> 00:53:31,833
But I'm also trying to figure out
where to put the other A

1058
00:53:31,917 --> 00:53:35,503
while counting squares to see
where all of the six-square sections end.

1059
00:53:36,171 --> 00:53:37,964
This could be over in just a couple turns.

1060
00:53:38,048 --> 00:53:39,591
Might last longer than that.

1061
00:53:39,674 --> 00:53:42,010
He could even open a D
to the right of the C

1062
00:53:42,093 --> 00:53:44,137
-and it would still probably work.
-Oh, that's true.

1063
00:53:44,221 --> 00:53:46,765
Real question is,
what's he gonna do about that A?

1064
00:53:46,848 --> 00:53:48,266
'Cause hell if I know.

1065
00:53:55,106 --> 00:53:56,858
Thirty seconds remain.

1066
00:53:58,777 --> 00:54:00,779
Did he just…

1067
00:54:00,862 --> 00:54:02,322
Shrinking the channels yet again.

1068
00:54:02,405 --> 00:54:04,616
-This is his thing, I guess.
-That takes balls.

1069
00:54:04,699 --> 00:54:07,077
Putting the A there
means only one additional pair

1070
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:10,664
can fit in the middle channel,
on the other side of the A path.

1071
00:54:10,747 --> 00:54:14,167
So now, if I can make it
so that only one more pair of letters

1072
00:54:14,251 --> 00:54:16,002
can fit in the outer channel,

1073
00:54:16,086 --> 00:54:17,879
then the win should fall on my turn.

1074
00:54:21,341 --> 00:54:22,592
Ten seconds remain.

1075
00:54:24,719 --> 00:54:27,639
Five, four, three…

1076
00:54:29,891 --> 00:54:31,726
-Whoa, shrunken down again.
-He's done it!

1077
00:54:31,810 --> 00:54:34,020
If the path goes around this way, and…

1078
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:36,564
the bottom left corner's taken up,

1079
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:37,649
-the game's over.
-Yeah.

1080
00:54:37,732 --> 00:54:41,027
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1081
00:54:55,667 --> 00:54:57,877
I like this game. Really draws you in.

1082
00:54:57,961 --> 00:55:00,714
-Yeah. I feel like I'm the one competing.
-Same here.

1083
00:55:22,402 --> 00:55:24,446
And now I'm immediately regretting it.

1084
00:55:24,529 --> 00:55:27,198
I shouldn't have put C
so close to B. I screwed up,

1085
00:55:27,282 --> 00:55:29,951
thinking too hard about that space
as a path for the B's.

1086
00:55:30,035 --> 00:55:32,203
He didn't realize
that the B could be closed off,

1087
00:55:32,287 --> 00:55:34,748
since he was so focused
on blocking the other pieces.

1088
00:55:34,831 --> 00:55:36,666
But he thought B would be
closed off to the left.

1089
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:40,128
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1090
00:55:50,889 --> 00:55:53,600
With that J placed down,
there's no other move he can make.

1091
00:55:53,683 --> 00:55:55,769
-Now Dong-min can declare impossibility.
-Yeah.

1092
00:55:55,852 --> 00:55:58,730
If he tried to open a new pair,
that'd be an instant violation.

1093
00:56:03,026 --> 00:56:06,029
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1094
00:56:06,112 --> 00:56:07,322
It's impossible.

1095
00:56:07,405 --> 00:56:09,741
Jang Dong-min has declared impossibility.

1096
00:56:09,824 --> 00:56:12,994
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you have five minutes
to prove the connections.

1097
00:56:13,078 --> 00:56:14,454
I forfeit.

1098
00:56:14,537 --> 00:56:17,874
<i>Since Hyun Kyung-lyul has failed</i>
<i>to prove the connections,</i>

1099
00:56:17,957 --> 00:56:21,086
<i>Jang Dong-min has earned himself</i>
<i>one point.</i>

1100
00:56:21,169 --> 00:56:23,671
You got this. Very nice.

1101
00:56:23,755 --> 00:56:25,965
-1-1.
-Wow, this is close.

1102
00:56:26,633 --> 00:56:28,093
Why did I do that?

1103
00:56:28,176 --> 00:56:29,427
All right, this time…

1104
00:56:30,553 --> 00:56:33,556
Kyung-lyul should've placed that C
just one square higher.

1105
00:56:33,640 --> 00:56:36,142
If he'd done that,
then left six squares underneath,

1106
00:56:36,226 --> 00:56:37,268
I think he would've won.

1107
00:56:37,352 --> 00:56:39,938
-Damn, this is fun.
-Dong-min's a god.

1108
00:56:40,021 --> 00:56:41,981
What in the world
is the next board gonna look like?

1109
00:56:42,065 --> 00:56:44,275
-Oh, yeah.
-Probably gonna be the craziest yet.

1110
00:56:44,359 --> 00:56:47,487
We will now begin round three.
Here is the board.

1111
00:56:48,822 --> 00:56:51,157
-Okay, this one's a brain-buster.
