1126
00:57:29,446 --> 00:57:30,947
One minute remains.

1127
00:57:38,246 --> 00:57:40,039
Having to start this one-off,

1128
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,375
if I start shrinking the board down
right out of the gate,

1129
00:57:42,459 --> 00:57:44,377
it's gonna be way harder for me
to maintain control.

1130
00:57:44,461 --> 00:57:47,714
So I placed it right at the end,
playing it safe for my opening move.

1131
00:57:47,797 --> 00:57:50,925
This way, I could keep
as many possibilities open as I can.

1132
00:57:51,009 --> 00:57:53,887
Doesn't that take out the diagonal strip
on the whole board?

1133
00:57:53,970 --> 00:57:57,974
Not completely. You could still shimmy up
the top edge of the space like this

1134
00:57:58,057 --> 00:58:00,185
and still have room
for at least a couple below it.

1135
00:58:00,268 --> 00:58:01,644
Ah. Uh-huh.

1136
00:58:01,728 --> 00:58:03,855
But Kyung-lyul's whole MO

1137
00:58:03,938 --> 00:58:06,232
-is to wipe out a huge chunk…
-…so he could make use of that J.

1138
00:58:06,316 --> 00:58:08,026
-Probably what he'll do.
-Yeah, yeah, he might…

1139
00:58:08,109 --> 00:58:09,777
The triangle's gonna be a war zone.

1140
00:58:10,487 --> 00:58:13,615
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1141
00:58:23,958 --> 00:58:26,002
-Yep, he's shrinking the board again.
-Yeah.

1142
00:58:26,085 --> 00:58:27,837
That whole section is out of play.

1143
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:39,265
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1144
00:58:45,396 --> 00:58:46,648
One minute remains.

1145
00:59:04,374 --> 00:59:07,502
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1146
00:59:37,282 --> 00:59:40,076
Wait, can you get six squares
if you put it there?

1147
00:59:40,159 --> 00:59:42,537
-If you do a U-turn, you totally can.
-Like this, yeah.

1148
00:59:42,620 --> 00:59:44,122
Oh, yeah, yeah, you're right.

1149
00:59:44,205 --> 00:59:45,248
-Wow.
-Is that it?

1150
00:59:45,331 --> 00:59:46,457
-They're done.
-It's over.

1151
00:59:46,541 --> 00:59:47,959
The B path just ended the round.

1152
01:00:00,388 --> 01:00:02,098
-What was that for?
-Huh?

1153
01:00:02,724 --> 01:00:04,517
Can he even fit that?

1154
01:00:04,601 --> 01:00:06,144
Why wouldn't he be able to?

1155
01:00:08,479 --> 01:00:10,607
I laid down B and C with real intent.

1156
01:00:10,690 --> 01:00:14,068
The X's are joined diagonally,
leaving space on the right for two pairs

1157
01:00:14,152 --> 01:00:16,529
and some space on the top for one pair.

1158
01:00:16,613 --> 01:00:19,574
Oh, I don't know if that works
with the B placed there. Does it?

1159
01:00:19,657 --> 01:00:21,451
It does if you zigzag.

1160
01:00:21,534 --> 01:00:22,994
Like in this kind of shape.

1161
01:00:23,703 --> 01:00:25,038
Oh, shit.

1162
01:00:25,121 --> 01:00:26,539
-You're so right.
-Oh, my God…

1163
01:00:26,623 --> 01:00:27,624
Huh.

1164
01:00:27,707 --> 01:00:29,250
-And just when you think…
-Crazy.

1165
01:00:29,334 --> 01:00:30,752
…you've got the puzzle figured out.

1166
01:00:31,961 --> 01:00:34,255
Good on Kyung-lyul for finding that spot.

1167
01:00:36,257 --> 01:00:37,717
I admit, I'm impressed.

1168
01:00:45,224 --> 01:00:47,101
Isn't it now impossible
to place anything else?

1169
01:00:47,185 --> 01:00:48,811
Now it doesn't matter
what move he makes. Ugh.

1170
01:00:48,895 --> 01:00:51,689
Tight squeeze, but he might
still be able to pull it off.

1171
01:00:57,111 --> 01:00:58,488
Ten seconds remain.

1172
01:00:59,906 --> 01:01:02,742
Five, four, three…

1173
01:01:02,825 --> 01:01:05,745
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1174
01:01:08,998 --> 01:01:10,416
I declare impossibility.

1175
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:12,835
Hyun Kyung-lyul has
declared impossibility.

1176
01:01:13,336 --> 01:01:16,589
Jang Dong-min, you have five minutes
to prove the connections.

1177
01:01:17,298 --> 01:01:20,134
Please place the matching piece
for the unpaired one,

1178
01:01:20,218 --> 01:01:21,761
and connect that pair as well.

1179
01:01:27,934 --> 01:01:29,435
Let's move to the next round.

1180
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:31,729
Jang Dong-min has forfeited the proof.

1181
01:01:32,313 --> 01:01:35,566
<i>Since Jang Dong-min has</i>
<i>failed to prove the connections,</i>

1182
01:01:35,650 --> 01:01:38,903
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul has earned himself</i>
<i>one point.</i>

1183
01:01:38,986 --> 01:01:40,613
Wow.

1184
01:01:41,406 --> 01:01:42,907
-Very good.
-Whew, now he's on fire.

1185
01:01:42,990 --> 01:01:44,742
-Yeah, finally.
-Kyung-lyul's amazing.

1186
01:01:45,576 --> 01:01:48,538
We now move to round four.
Here is the board.

1187
01:01:49,706 --> 01:01:51,249
Ah, it just got harder.

1188
01:01:52,083 --> 01:01:53,668
-Wow.
-It's a big blank slate.

1189
01:01:53,751 --> 01:01:56,212
-Damn. It's got, like, nothing on it.
-Wow.

1190
01:01:56,295 --> 01:01:59,549
Jang Dong-min, please choose
who will take the first turn.

1191
01:02:01,300 --> 01:02:02,885
I'll be going second.

1192
01:02:02,969 --> 01:02:05,972
I chose to be the second player,
and yet, I'm still feeling like,

1193
01:02:06,556 --> 01:02:08,975
"Geez, why am I being penalized
with this wide open board

1194
01:02:09,058 --> 01:02:11,185
when I'm the one who gets to go second?"

1195
01:02:11,269 --> 01:02:13,646
Still, I think I can
take control of this one.

1196
01:02:14,439 --> 01:02:16,691
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you have three minutes

1197
01:02:16,774 --> 01:02:18,484
to place your first piece.

1198
01:02:19,527 --> 01:02:21,112
Let's just put it anywhere.

1199
01:02:23,197 --> 01:02:25,074
Ah, right in the middle.

1200
01:02:25,158 --> 01:02:27,243
Can't really strategize yet anyway.

1201
01:02:27,326 --> 01:02:30,371
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1202
01:02:39,046 --> 01:02:40,840
Oh, God.

1203
01:02:40,923 --> 01:02:42,717
Now that's interesting.

1204
01:02:42,800 --> 01:02:45,511
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1205
01:02:57,315 --> 01:02:59,650
Okay, so with the A and the B there,

1206
01:02:59,734 --> 01:03:02,195
already the board's been divided in two.

1207
01:03:02,278 --> 01:03:04,155
-Right, so then you…
-Whichever way you go…

1208
01:03:04,238 --> 01:03:06,532
You can split the board
from above or below.

1209
01:03:06,616 --> 01:03:10,328
I think he likes to start by reducing
the number of possibilities.

1210
01:03:10,411 --> 01:03:12,997
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1211
01:03:27,512 --> 01:03:29,055
Thirty seconds remain.

1212
01:03:29,138 --> 01:03:31,933
Having a totally empty board
is way harder than it looks.

1213
01:03:34,101 --> 01:03:36,813
Five, four, three…

1214
01:03:37,897 --> 01:03:39,899
-Carving it down as he goes.
-Mmm.

1215
01:03:39,982 --> 01:03:42,527
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1216
01:03:51,369 --> 01:03:54,247
I'm sure we're both
mapping out the paths in our heads.

1217
01:03:54,330 --> 01:03:55,665
So you've gotta think about the path

1218
01:03:55,748 --> 01:03:57,834
your opponent is mapping out
and block 'em off

1219
01:03:57,917 --> 01:04:00,336
in order to force them
to come up with something else.

1220
01:04:04,507 --> 01:04:05,967
Already countered it.

1221
01:04:06,884 --> 01:04:09,387
Now the D path
has to wrap around the left side.

1222
01:04:09,470 --> 01:04:12,640
If it doesn't go around that perimeter,
it'll cut off the B path.

1223
01:04:12,723 --> 01:04:13,766
Hmm.

1224
01:04:13,850 --> 01:04:15,434
Unless the B path comes straight down--

1225
01:04:15,518 --> 01:04:17,061
The B path wrapping around works too.

1226
01:04:17,144 --> 01:04:19,355
The C's and A's can join from above,

1227
01:04:20,273 --> 01:04:21,774
the B's from below,

1228
01:04:21,858 --> 01:04:25,403
and the D's can be joined in the three
vertical lines with plenty of space.

1229
01:04:25,486 --> 01:04:28,322
Still a lot more possibilities
than it would seem.

1230
01:04:28,406 --> 01:04:31,325
Even though they definitely
reduced them with those placements.

1231
01:04:37,456 --> 01:04:39,667
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1232
01:04:40,835 --> 01:04:41,919
There's still way too many.

1233
01:04:42,003 --> 01:04:44,171
Yeah, they really
got to narrow things down.

1234
01:04:49,677 --> 01:04:52,179
-Huh?
-He cut off another path.

1235
01:04:52,263 --> 01:04:55,308
Now, the B path
has to wrap around, doesn't it?

1236
01:04:58,311 --> 01:05:01,063
Five, four, three…

1237
01:05:02,398 --> 01:05:04,442
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1238
01:05:20,041 --> 01:05:21,334
Thirty seconds remain.

1239
01:05:23,628 --> 01:05:26,714
There you go,
filled up all that empty space.

1240
01:05:26,797 --> 01:05:30,468
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1241
01:05:38,225 --> 01:05:40,895
Five, four, three…

1242
01:05:41,687 --> 01:05:43,397
He just squished them together.

1243
01:05:43,481 --> 01:05:45,733
Yeah, to take up that whole corner.

1244
01:05:45,816 --> 01:05:48,694
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1245
01:06:01,874 --> 01:06:03,167
-That's it.
-Good.

1246
01:06:03,250 --> 01:06:04,919
Got rid of more empty spaces.

1247
01:06:05,419 --> 01:06:08,130
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1248
01:06:16,430 --> 01:06:19,558
I feel like we're just about
to see a genius move.

1249
01:06:26,273 --> 01:06:27,775
Oh, wait a sec.

1250
01:06:28,526 --> 01:06:31,529
Can you even fit six squares in there?

1251
01:06:31,612 --> 01:06:34,031
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1252
01:06:41,205 --> 01:06:42,498
-Wait…
-Huh?

1253
01:06:43,332 --> 01:06:44,792
Does that work?

1254
01:06:44,875 --> 01:06:46,752
Maybe there's something we're missing.

1255
01:06:56,012 --> 01:06:58,723
Jang Dong-min, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1256
01:07:10,985 --> 01:07:14,238
I think he's got it,
but he keeps on double-checking his work.

1257
01:07:16,323 --> 01:07:17,575
It's impossible.

1258
01:07:17,658 --> 01:07:19,952
-Oh, he declared it again.
-Declared another impossibility.

1259
01:07:21,704 --> 01:07:24,248
Yo, he whipped out that pen
right away. He's ready.

1260
01:07:24,331 --> 01:07:26,417
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you have five minutes

1261
01:07:26,500 --> 01:07:27,835
to prove the connections.

1262
01:07:29,837 --> 01:07:31,839
Man, no hesitation.

1263
01:07:31,922 --> 01:07:33,424
I think he's got it. Look at him go.

1264
01:07:33,507 --> 01:07:35,384
Yeah, and how quick he's marking it up.

1265
01:07:48,522 --> 01:07:51,442
-Oh.
-Oh, the F path doesn't work.

1266
01:07:51,525 --> 01:07:54,653
-The B path doesn't leave any room for it.
-Ugh.

1267
01:07:58,991 --> 01:08:01,160
If Kyung-lyul hadn't placed the K there,

1268
01:08:01,243 --> 01:08:02,953
all the connections would've worked.

1269
01:08:06,707 --> 01:08:09,627
But I'm 100% sure,
this layout's impossible.

1270
01:08:09,710 --> 01:08:11,295
Nice, God Dong-min.

1271
01:08:12,713 --> 01:08:14,256
It's gonna be five rounds.

1272
01:08:14,340 --> 01:08:15,925
Bet he's already mentally preparing

1273
01:08:16,008 --> 01:08:17,676
-for the next one.
-For sure.

1274
01:08:17,760 --> 01:08:22,431
Five, four, three, two, one.

1275
01:08:22,515 --> 01:08:23,891
Your time is up.

1276
01:08:23,974 --> 01:08:27,228
Yeah, sad to say, that last move
I made was a really bad one.

1277
01:08:27,728 --> 01:08:29,563
I was agonizing over my moves so much

1278
01:08:29,647 --> 01:08:32,024
I had two different images
overlapping in my head.

1279
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:33,859
And then right when I went up to bat,

1280
01:08:33,943 --> 01:08:36,237
I drew the incorrect one
of those two images.

1281
01:08:36,737 --> 01:08:39,990
<i>As Hyun Kyung-lyul has failed</i>
<i>to prove the connections,</i>

1282
01:08:40,074 --> 01:08:43,035
<i>Jang Dong-min has earned himself</i>
<i>another point.</i>

1283
01:08:44,078 --> 01:08:46,705
Wow. Now this is a match.

1284
01:08:46,789 --> 01:08:49,375
And if they're tied right now,
the next round's the last.

1285
01:08:54,130 --> 01:08:55,256
I got this.

1286
01:08:57,424 --> 01:08:59,468
The fifth and final round begins.

1287
01:08:59,552 --> 01:09:00,803
Yeah, here we go!

1288
01:09:00,886 --> 01:09:02,638
-Bring it on.
-Bring it!

1289
01:09:02,721 --> 01:09:04,473
Here is the last board.

1290
01:09:10,104 --> 01:09:12,106
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you have three minutes

1291
01:09:12,189 --> 01:09:13,649
to choose the player order.

1292
01:09:13,732 --> 01:09:15,818
Given where
the X's and the Y's are placed,

1293
01:09:15,901 --> 01:09:18,028
the top and bottom sections
are totally separate.

1294
01:09:18,112 --> 01:09:21,740
So this board is all about
keeping track of both square counts.

1295
01:09:21,824 --> 01:09:23,075
I'd like to go second.

1296
01:09:23,159 --> 01:09:24,702
You have chosen to go second.

1297
01:09:25,369 --> 01:09:27,663
Jang Dong-min,
you will be the first player.

1298
01:09:27,746 --> 01:09:30,833
You have three minutes
to place your first piece.

1299
01:09:30,916 --> 01:09:32,751
Their brains have got
to be exhausted by now.

1300
01:09:32,835 --> 01:09:34,712
-Yeah, they must be fried.
-Hungry too.

1301
01:09:34,795 --> 01:09:36,463
They've just gotta concentrate.

1302
01:09:36,547 --> 01:09:39,300
When it comes to brain power, those two?

1303
01:09:39,383 --> 01:09:40,384
They'll be just fine.

1304
01:09:40,467 --> 01:09:43,679
Even making it to the final
round is super impressive by itself.

1305
01:09:53,689 --> 01:09:55,900
Oh, I know exactly what I did.

1306
01:09:55,983 --> 01:09:59,320
I placed the A there as a way
of delineating the two sections,

1307
01:09:59,403 --> 01:10:01,655
so we'll see how he deals with that.

1308
01:10:01,739 --> 01:10:03,324
-Ooh…
-Whoa!

1309
01:10:03,407 --> 01:10:04,867
-That's nasty.
-Blocked it off.

1310
01:10:04,950 --> 01:10:08,370
Probably had the same idea
to clog that up before anything else.

1311
01:10:09,121 --> 01:10:10,998
But now what's left to do?

1312
01:10:11,749 --> 01:10:14,835
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1313
01:10:21,800 --> 01:10:23,552
Ambiguous spot for the A.

1314
01:10:23,636 --> 01:10:26,055
That placement's best for a path
that goes along the top,

1315
01:10:26,138 --> 01:10:27,890
up one space and then back down.

1316
01:10:27,973 --> 01:10:30,184
But that's still seven spaces at minimum.

1317
01:10:30,267 --> 01:10:31,852
Sure, but seven's not bad.

1318
01:10:32,478 --> 01:10:35,105
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1319
01:10:52,456 --> 01:10:54,541
Now that I've split the board in two,

1320
01:10:54,625 --> 01:10:57,169
if Kyung-lyul throws down even numbers,

1321
01:10:57,253 --> 01:10:59,463
I make 'em into odd numbers.

1322
01:10:59,546 --> 01:11:03,133
That's how I'm keeping track
of the number of possibilities.

1323
01:11:03,217 --> 01:11:04,510
Thirty seconds remain.

1324
01:11:09,390 --> 01:11:11,850
He's figured out the maximum number
of pairs that can fit,

1325
01:11:11,934 --> 01:11:14,311
and now he's placing everything
in the optimal positions.

1326
01:11:14,937 --> 01:11:16,272
-That makes sense.
-Mmm.

1327
01:11:16,355 --> 01:11:18,649
He's checking if Kyung-lyul
is seeing the same paths as him.

1328
01:11:18,732 --> 01:11:20,693
He's got to force him
to follow the same ones.

1329
01:11:20,776 --> 01:11:23,612
He's already mapped out
all the paths for A, B, C and D,

1330
01:11:23,696 --> 01:11:25,698
so if Kyung-lyul encroaches
on any of them,

1331
01:11:25,781 --> 01:11:27,157
he'll have to declare an impossibility.

1332
01:11:27,241 --> 01:11:28,826
Right. Exactly the case.

1333
01:11:28,909 --> 01:11:30,160
Good strategy.

1334
01:11:30,244 --> 01:11:33,289
Ah, so Kyung-lyul's gotta keep looking
for the paths that'll work.

1335
01:11:33,372 --> 01:11:35,040
Yep, he's gonna have a rough time.

1336
01:11:35,124 --> 01:11:38,294
Hyun Kyung-lyul, it's your turn.
Please place two pieces.

1337
01:11:49,096 --> 01:11:51,849
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1338
01:11:54,560 --> 01:11:56,520
His next move could change it all.

1339
01:11:57,104 --> 01:12:00,566
I think this is where the order of play
is gonna benefit Dong-min.

1340
01:12:01,150 --> 01:12:02,401
Thirty seconds remain.

1341
01:12:14,663 --> 01:12:16,040
Ten seconds remain.

1342
01:12:19,418 --> 01:12:23,839
Five, four, three, two, one.

1343
01:12:25,716 --> 01:12:27,343
Now the X path on the left's closed.

1344
01:12:27,426 --> 01:12:29,219
And now for the E path to work,

1345
01:12:29,303 --> 01:12:31,430
it'd have to curve a little
around the top.

1346
01:12:31,513 --> 01:12:34,350
-And the Y path has to curve too.
-Oh, now I see what you mean.

1347
01:12:34,433 --> 01:12:36,685
Oh… Yeah, that'll be tricky.

1348
01:12:36,769 --> 01:12:39,563
Hyun Kyung-lyul, please place two pieces.

1349
01:12:46,528 --> 01:12:48,989
Kyung-lyul's heart
must be ready to explode.

1350
01:12:49,073 --> 01:12:51,241
Yeah, if he doesn't take this round…

1351
01:12:51,325 --> 01:12:53,952
-This turn will be his last…
-And then it's all done.

1352
01:12:54,036 --> 01:12:56,997
Let's not forget, he's got 200 mil
riding on this one moment.

1353
01:12:57,081 --> 01:12:59,083
-No pressure or anything.
-So true.

1354
01:12:59,166 --> 01:13:01,543
Brain's gotta be melting
thinking two moves ahead.

1355
01:13:02,628 --> 01:13:03,921
Thirty seconds remain.

1356
01:13:07,508 --> 01:13:09,676
After that last move Dong-min made,

1357
01:13:09,760 --> 01:13:12,638
from my calculations,
there's no way I can win.

1358
01:13:13,472 --> 01:13:15,516
All I could think was,
"What can I even do here?"

1359
01:13:17,643 --> 01:13:19,019
Ten seconds remain.

1360
01:13:26,151 --> 01:13:29,321
Five, four, three, two…

1361
01:13:31,740 --> 01:13:33,075
Damn, they're both good.

1362
01:13:33,158 --> 01:13:34,868
Definition of a clash of the titans.

1363
01:13:34,952 --> 01:13:36,036
You said a mouthful.

1364
01:13:36,120 --> 01:13:38,664
Jang Dong-min, please place two pieces.

1365
01:13:51,635 --> 01:13:52,845
It's impossible.

1366
01:13:54,221 --> 01:13:56,974
Jang Dong-min has declared impossibility.

1367
01:13:58,892 --> 01:14:00,310
-Huh?
-Huh?

1368
01:14:04,189 --> 01:14:06,150
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you have five minutes

1369
01:14:06,233 --> 01:14:07,860
to prove the connections.

1370
01:14:16,452 --> 01:14:18,912
Please place the matching piece
for the unpaired one

1371
01:14:18,996 --> 01:14:20,831
before you complete your proof.

1372
01:14:34,845 --> 01:14:36,263
No way.

1373
01:14:37,598 --> 01:14:39,892
Hold up,
I think he might have figured it out.

1374
01:14:44,771 --> 01:14:46,565
Place the matching piece for F.

1375
01:14:49,151 --> 01:14:51,987
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul has</i>
<i>successfully proven the connections</i>

1376
01:14:52,070 --> 01:14:53,238
<i>and has earned himself one point.</i>

1377
01:14:53,322 --> 01:14:54,656
How did I not catch that?

1378
01:14:54,740 --> 01:14:57,993
<i>The final score is 3-2,</i>
<i>in favor of Hyun Kyung-lyul.</i>

1379
01:14:58,076 --> 01:15:01,663
<i>Therefore, Hyun Kyung-lyul</i>
<i>is victorious in the second game</i>

1380
01:15:01,747 --> 01:15:03,457
<i>of the final match.</i>

1381
01:15:04,082 --> 01:15:05,542
Wow!

1382
01:15:05,626 --> 01:15:07,753
-My God…
-Dong-min didn't see it coming.

1383
01:15:07,836 --> 01:15:09,087
Oh, he missed it, all right.

1384
01:15:09,171 --> 01:15:12,466
-Couldn't have expected that. Wow.
-Wow. Hot damn.

1385
01:15:13,050 --> 01:15:14,968
-Ugh.
-Wow.

1386
01:15:15,052 --> 01:15:17,095
Closing off the D
was just a throwaway move,

1387
01:15:17,179 --> 01:15:20,224
and then I placed the F
to make the E's look a bit iffy.

1388
01:15:20,307 --> 01:15:23,227
I figured he might neglect to account
for the squares up in that corner,

1389
01:15:23,310 --> 01:15:25,103
so that's why I put the F up there.

1390
01:15:25,938 --> 01:15:28,232
How did I miss that shit?

1391
01:15:28,315 --> 01:15:30,317
Ugh, I should've checked that corner.

1392
01:15:30,901 --> 01:15:33,862
I would've seen that move.
But I got too careless.

1393
01:15:33,946 --> 01:15:35,614
Even he's capable of slipping up,

1394
01:15:35,697 --> 01:15:38,825
which means I've got a real shot
of beating him in the final game.

1395
01:15:39,451 --> 01:15:41,828
-Well played.
-Thanks. One more to go.

1396
01:15:41,912 --> 01:15:42,913
Mmm.

1397
01:15:42,996 --> 01:15:46,333
<i>The third and final game</i>
<i>will begin shortly.</i>

1398
01:15:47,084 --> 01:15:50,212
Hey, until I hear the words,
"Jang Dong-min is the winner,"

1399
01:15:50,295 --> 01:15:51,964
it's not over yet.

1400
01:15:52,047 --> 01:15:54,716
That's why I lost. I got ahead of myself.

1401
01:15:54,800 --> 01:15:59,096
I thought… I thought I had already won,
but that made me lose.

1402
01:16:05,477 --> 01:16:09,022
<i>And now, I'll explain the rules</i>
<i>of the third game.</i>

1403
01:16:09,106 --> 01:16:14,152
<i>The last game of the final match</i>
<i>is Equation Traffic Light.</i>

1404
01:16:14,736 --> 01:16:17,864
<i>In Equation Traffic Light,</i>
<i>you must use color clues</i>

1405
01:16:17,948 --> 01:16:21,535
<i>to figure out the equation</i>
<i>your opponent has created.</i>

1406
01:16:21,618 --> 01:16:22,619
What?

1407
01:16:22,703 --> 01:16:24,079
<i>Once the game begins,</i>

1408
01:16:24,162 --> 01:16:27,916
<i>the two of you will have five minutes</i>
<i>to create a nine-cell equation,</i>

1409
01:16:28,000 --> 01:16:30,627
<i>which will be hidden</i>
<i>from your opponent upon submission.</i>

1410
01:16:31,295 --> 01:16:32,629
Aw, shit.

1411
01:16:34,047 --> 01:16:37,467
<i>You may, of course,</i>
<i>use the numbers zero through nine,</i>

1412
01:16:37,551 --> 01:16:41,305
<i>as well as the symbols</i>
<i>for addition, subtraction,</i>

1413
01:16:41,388 --> 01:16:45,934
<i>multiplication, division,</i>
<i>equals and exponent.</i>

1414
01:16:46,643 --> 01:16:48,520
Oh, they got exponents now.

1415
01:16:48,604 --> 01:16:50,314
<i>This should go without saying,</i>

1416
01:16:50,397 --> 01:16:52,858
<i>but the equation must be</i>
<i>mathematically valid.</i>

1417
01:16:53,859 --> 01:16:57,821
<i>You are permitted to use the same number</i>
<i>or symbol more than once,</i>

1418
01:16:57,904 --> 01:17:01,074
<i>but you may not place two symbols</i>
<i>next to each other.</i>

1419
01:17:01,867 --> 01:17:05,078
<i>You must include the multiplication symbol</i>
<i>when multiplying,</i>

1420
01:17:05,162 --> 01:17:08,290
<i>and a number must always</i>
<i>follow the exponent symbol.</i>

1421
01:17:09,958 --> 01:17:12,794
<i>Also, you may not write</i>
<i>a single-digit number</i>

1422
01:17:12,878 --> 01:17:14,296
<i>with a leading zero.</i>

1423
01:17:14,379 --> 01:17:16,048
<i>Please keep this in mind.</i>

1424
01:17:17,174 --> 01:17:19,843
<i>Once both of your equations</i>
<i>have been submitted,</i>

1425
01:17:19,926 --> 01:17:23,221
<i>each of you will try to guess</i>
<i>your opponent's equation.</i>

1426
01:17:24,306 --> 01:17:28,185
<i>You will have five minutes to combine</i>
<i>the numbers and symbols listed earlier</i>

1427
01:17:28,268 --> 01:17:30,062
<i>and submit your answer.</i>

1428
01:17:30,145 --> 01:17:34,858
<i>Take note: Your answer does not need</i>
<i>to be a mathematically-valid equation.</i>

1429
01:17:35,942 --> 01:17:37,819
<i>Once both answers have been submitted,</i>

1430
01:17:37,903 --> 01:17:40,280
<i>the answers will be shown</i>
<i>with each cell marked</i>

1431
01:17:40,364 --> 01:17:42,699
<i>with one of three types of color clues.</i>

1432
01:17:43,742 --> 01:17:46,828
<i>The color red indicates</i>
<i>that the number or symbol</i>

1433
01:17:46,912 --> 01:17:49,206
<i>is not in the original equation.</i>

1434
01:17:50,207 --> 01:17:52,876
<i>The color yellow indicates</i>
<i>that the number or symbol</i>

1435
01:17:52,959 --> 01:17:55,212
<i>is included in the original equation,</i>

1436
01:17:55,295 --> 01:17:57,172
<i>but in a different position.</i>

1437
01:17:57,255 --> 01:18:00,509
<i>And the color green indicates</i>
<i>that the number or symbol is,</i>

1438
01:18:00,592 --> 01:18:02,511
<i>in fact, in the correct position.</i>

1439
01:18:04,554 --> 01:18:09,267
<i>Further, if your answer contains</i>
<i>a multiple of the same number or symbol,</i>

1440
01:18:09,351 --> 01:18:11,895
<i>but the original equation only has one,</i>

1441
01:18:12,646 --> 01:18:15,691
<i>then one of them</i>
<i>will be marked green or yellow,</i>

1442
01:18:15,774 --> 01:18:17,484
<i>depending on its position,</i>

1443
01:18:17,567 --> 01:18:19,903
<i>and the rest will be marked in red.</i>

1444
01:18:20,737 --> 01:18:24,241
<i>If you do not submit an answer</i>
<i>within the time limit,</i>

1445
01:18:24,324 --> 01:18:26,993
<i>you will not receive any clues.</i>

1446
01:18:28,286 --> 01:18:30,789
<i>You will then be allowed</i>
<i>another five minutes</i>

1447
01:18:30,872 --> 01:18:34,584
<i>to submit a new answer</i>
<i>using the clues you've received.</i>

1448
01:18:35,627 --> 01:18:38,839
<i>This process will repeat</i>
<i>until one of the two players</i>

1449
01:18:38,922 --> 01:18:41,842
<i>correctly guesses the other's equation.</i>

1450
01:18:42,509 --> 01:18:46,388
<i>That player will be crowned</i>
<i>the final winner of </i>The Devil's Plan.

1451
01:18:47,013 --> 01:18:48,223
-Oh.
-That's it.

1452
01:18:48,306 --> 01:18:50,267
-It's one round?
-Oh, this is really it.

1453
01:18:50,350 --> 01:18:51,768
-A single round.
-Yeah.

1454
01:18:53,603 --> 01:18:57,357
<i>In the event that both players</i>
<i>guess correctly at the same time,</i>

1455
01:18:57,441 --> 01:19:00,902
<i>you will play again</i>
<i>until a single winner can be determined.</i>

1456
01:19:01,778 --> 01:19:03,113
<i>Prepare yourselves.</i>

1457
01:19:03,196 --> 01:19:06,616
<i>The final game of the final match</i>
<i>will begin shortly.</i>

1458
01:19:06,700 --> 01:19:09,327
This one would be fun
to play together at home.

1459
01:19:09,411 --> 01:19:11,621
-How do you make it as complex as you can?
-Right?

1460
01:19:11,705 --> 01:19:12,873
The thing is…

1461
01:19:13,540 --> 01:19:15,167
it doesn't have to be impossible to solve.

1462
01:19:15,250 --> 01:19:18,378
It's more important to make it difficult
to guess with what you can use.

1463
01:19:18,462 --> 01:19:21,131
Like, if it were me playing,
for my first attempt,

1464
01:19:21,214 --> 01:19:23,633
I'd pick three cells that would be
unlikely to have numbers,

1465
01:19:23,717 --> 01:19:25,594
stick some numbers in each of those,

1466
01:19:25,677 --> 01:19:27,888
and then fill the rest
with the six symbols.

1467
01:19:27,971 --> 01:19:29,890
And finally I'd plug in
the rest of the numbers

1468
01:19:29,973 --> 01:19:31,099
while picking their positions.

1469
01:19:31,183 --> 01:19:32,893
Pretty simple to figure out the equation.

1470
01:19:32,976 --> 01:19:36,480
Ah. How you figure them out
is important too.

1471
01:19:37,522 --> 01:19:39,191
I already know the key to this one

1472
01:19:39,274 --> 01:19:41,651
is the position of the equal sign.

1473
01:19:41,735 --> 01:19:44,780
Seriously. Figuring out
that symbol's position is imperative.

1474
01:19:44,863 --> 01:19:47,949
Once you know where it is,
the rest of the equation is easy.

1475
01:19:48,033 --> 01:19:50,118
But what's equally important to that

1476
01:19:50,202 --> 01:19:52,537
is being able to read
your opponent's assessment of you

1477
01:19:52,621 --> 01:19:56,917
because then you can determine how likely
they are to be able to trick you.

1478
01:19:57,000 --> 01:19:58,502
Hey, I just had a question.

1479
01:19:58,585 --> 01:20:00,295
So if it's the standard
order of operations

1480
01:20:00,378 --> 01:20:02,422
for A times B to the power of C,

1481
01:20:02,506 --> 01:20:05,050
do you do B to the power of C first,
and then multiply A?

1482
01:20:05,133 --> 01:20:07,803
-You do the exponent first. Correct.
-That's what I thought.

1483
01:20:08,428 --> 01:20:11,139
I'd say it's pretty advantageous
to use the same numbers

1484
01:20:11,223 --> 01:20:12,849
or symbols multiple times,

1485
01:20:12,933 --> 01:20:14,851
since it increases
the number of possibilities

1486
01:20:14,935 --> 01:20:17,479
and it makes it harder
to figure out what goes where.

1487
01:20:17,562 --> 01:20:20,565
That said, Dong-min's probably
come to the same conclusion.

1488
01:20:20,649 --> 01:20:22,984
<i>Finalists, your time is up.</i>

1489
01:20:23,068 --> 01:20:25,487
<i>Please make your way down to the hall.</i>

1490
01:20:25,570 --> 01:20:28,448
No need to be nervous
just because it's the last game.

1491
01:20:28,532 --> 01:20:31,618
If I do my thing
and make good use of my psychology,

1492
01:20:31,701 --> 01:20:34,496
I have no doubt
that I can win this whole thing.

1493
01:20:34,579 --> 01:20:36,665
Mistakes might happen
because of how nerve-racking

1494
01:20:36,748 --> 01:20:38,041
the final round's gonna be.

1495
01:20:38,124 --> 01:20:41,169
Not just me.
Even Dong-min could get shaken up.

1496
01:20:41,253 --> 01:20:43,630
So I'm just gonna think positive
and lock in.

1497
01:20:43,713 --> 01:20:47,759
<i>Jang Dong-min and Hyun Kyung-lyul</i>
<i>are currently tied 1-1.</i>

1498
01:20:48,301 --> 01:20:50,428
<i>Therefore, whoever wins this game</i>

1499
01:20:50,512 --> 01:20:53,598
<i>will be the final winner</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan.

1500
01:20:53,682 --> 01:20:55,767
-Let's go!
-Good luck, guys.

1501
01:20:55,851 --> 01:20:58,103
-This is it.
-Come on, come on!

1502
01:20:58,186 --> 01:21:01,147
<i>With that, let us begin the final game:</i>

1503
01:21:01,231 --> 01:21:03,233
<i>Equation Traffic Light.</i>

1504
01:21:03,859 --> 01:21:05,902
You have five minutes
to create your equation,

1505
01:21:05,986 --> 01:21:07,904
which will be kept hidden
from your opponent.

1506
01:21:16,246 --> 01:21:17,706
How are they gonna do this?

1507
01:21:17,789 --> 01:21:19,916
I ain't got a clue. I can't even imagine.

1508
01:21:24,087 --> 01:21:27,716
Starting off, an equation
like this one could probably be guessed

1509
01:21:27,799 --> 01:21:29,175
in three tries.

1510
01:21:29,259 --> 01:21:32,804
Maybe even four or five at the max.
That's what I think.

1511
01:21:32,888 --> 01:21:35,599
And then, it'd be smart
to allow for one extra attempt

1512
01:21:35,682 --> 01:21:39,603
in case the combination of numbers gets
messed up or something along the way.

1513
01:21:41,771 --> 01:21:43,940
To give myself a good advantage,

1514
01:21:44,024 --> 01:21:47,152
I'm trying to come up with an equation
that uses a lot of the same numbers,

1515
01:21:47,235 --> 01:21:49,446
which ought to make it harder
for him to figure out.

1516
01:21:54,200 --> 01:21:56,536
Both of your equations
have been submitted.

1517
01:21:56,620 --> 01:21:59,748
You each have five minutes
to guess your opponent's equation.

1518
01:21:59,831 --> 01:22:02,834
Place your answer in front of the screen
before time is up.

1519
01:22:03,919 --> 01:22:06,129
My angle is to put together an answer

1520
01:22:06,212 --> 01:22:08,340
with numbers where
they'd make sense to be placed,

1521
01:22:08,423 --> 01:22:10,967
and the equal sign
where it would most likely be.

1522
01:22:14,554 --> 01:22:17,182
For my first guess, I'm just
jotting down one of each symbol

1523
01:22:17,265 --> 01:22:19,684
to figure out which ones
he did and didn't use.

1524
01:22:19,768 --> 01:22:22,646
Then, I'm filling the remaining spaces
with zero, one, two and three

1525
01:22:22,729 --> 01:22:24,314
to see which numbers are in there.

1526
01:22:24,397 --> 01:22:27,108
So basically, a sacrificial turn
to feel things out.

1527
01:22:27,192 --> 01:22:30,403
What would make it harder to guess,
using three symbols or four?

1528
01:22:30,487 --> 01:22:33,865
I think the positions would all be fixed.
If it's four, that is.

1529
01:22:33,949 --> 01:22:35,492
-Yeah.
-But if it's three,

1530
01:22:35,575 --> 01:22:37,744
-would it take an extra guess…
-I think three's a better choice.

1531
01:22:37,827 --> 01:22:39,496
Mmm, yeah, three might be better.

1532
01:22:39,579 --> 01:22:41,915
-So that's six numbers?
-Plus the equal sign's gotta be there too.

1533
01:22:41,998 --> 01:22:44,084
Place your answer in front of your screen.

1534
01:22:53,843 --> 01:22:55,720
We all know the equal sign's in there,

1535
01:22:55,804 --> 01:22:57,555
since an equation always has to have one.

1536
01:22:57,639 --> 01:23:00,225
So based on the positioning
of all the other symbols,

1537
01:23:00,308 --> 01:23:01,601
you can figure it out.

1538
01:23:01,685 --> 01:23:04,312
He didn't need to use the equal sign,
but did it anyway.

1539
01:23:04,396 --> 01:23:07,148
Yeah, he might still be trying
to figure out where it goes.

1540
01:23:07,232 --> 01:23:09,651
You guys think the equal sign's
gonna be on the left?

1541
01:23:09,734 --> 01:23:12,278
Yeah, you can throw off
your opponent with that.

1542
01:23:12,362 --> 01:23:15,281
I think left's definitely
a better place for the equal sign.

1543
01:23:15,365 --> 01:23:17,075
Here are your color clues.

1544
01:23:21,579 --> 01:23:22,831
Plus, one, two.

1545
01:23:24,833 --> 01:23:25,834
Plus…

1546
01:23:26,960 --> 01:23:28,378
I seriously couldn't believe

1547
01:23:28,461 --> 01:23:31,965
that I didn't get a single number correct
on my first guess.

1548
01:23:32,048 --> 01:23:35,510
And now that basically leaves
only four possible numbers.

1549
01:23:35,593 --> 01:23:37,679
-Oh, he's lookin' real strong right now.
-There aren't, uh…

1550
01:23:37,762 --> 01:23:39,597
Kyung-lyul hasn't used
many numbers at all.

1551
01:23:39,681 --> 01:23:41,558
I think his equation's
mostly playing around

1552
01:23:41,641 --> 01:23:43,018
with a bunch of zeros and ones.

1553
01:23:43,101 --> 01:23:45,228
Both players, you now have five minutes

1554
01:23:45,311 --> 01:23:47,605
to guess your opponent's equation.

1555
01:23:47,689 --> 01:23:49,941
Minus. Division.

1556
01:23:51,026 --> 01:23:53,445
By now, I have to figure out
his equation's got a one, a two,

1557
01:23:53,528 --> 01:23:55,947
an exponent symbol, and the addition sign.

1558
01:23:56,031 --> 01:23:58,825
So next, I need to determine
which numbers, from four through nine,

1559
01:23:58,908 --> 01:24:01,536
are in there,
then I'll only have three cells left.

1560
01:24:01,619 --> 01:24:05,248
Just from this turn, I can use all that
to find the positions of the symbols.

1561
01:24:07,959 --> 01:24:10,003
Dude, Kyung-lyul's fast.

1562
01:24:10,086 --> 01:24:11,504
-He's really fast.
-Mm, he's good.

1563
01:24:12,630 --> 01:24:13,882
How much time left?

1564
01:24:13,965 --> 01:24:15,842
Two and a half minutes remain.

1565
01:24:20,096 --> 01:24:21,514
Ten seconds remain.

1566
01:24:25,518 --> 01:24:28,313
Time is up. Place your final answer
in front of your screen.

1567
01:24:36,654 --> 01:24:38,990
Since the position
of the equal sign's so important,

1568
01:24:39,074 --> 01:24:42,077
I included it again.
We'll see how it goes.

1569
01:24:43,161 --> 01:24:44,370
He chose it again?

1570
01:24:44,454 --> 01:24:47,624
Dong-min knows that the position
of the equal sign is the key.

1571
01:24:47,707 --> 01:24:49,209
Here are your color clues.

1572
01:24:54,798 --> 01:24:57,300
-See? He already sniffed it out.
-They've both uncovered a lot.

1573
01:24:57,383 --> 01:24:59,594
His answer is a two-digit number.

1574
01:24:59,677 --> 01:25:01,971
-And Kyung-lyul's starts with a nine.
-Uh-huh.

1575
01:25:02,055 --> 01:25:04,516
-So he's only used zero, one and nine.
-Mmm.

1576
01:25:04,599 --> 01:25:07,310
You have five minutes
to come up with your answer.

1577
01:25:11,898 --> 01:25:14,067
I found
the exact position of the equal sign,

1578
01:25:14,150 --> 01:25:17,028
and I know his equation
starts with a nine.

1579
01:25:17,112 --> 01:25:18,238
But there's more to it.

1580
01:25:18,321 --> 01:25:21,866
The only numbers he's got
are a nine, a one and a zero.

1581
01:25:22,492 --> 01:25:26,996
And the symbols he's integrated
are an exponent and a multiplier.

1582
01:25:27,080 --> 01:25:31,251
So therefore, it's a two-digit number
that doesn't end in a zero.

1583
01:25:31,334 --> 01:25:35,755
And I've deduced it cannot be an 11,
and obviously not a zero-zero,

1584
01:25:35,839 --> 01:25:37,674
so it's gotta be 91.

1585
01:25:40,802 --> 01:25:43,680
-Wow, Dong-min's almost got it.
-You think?

1586
01:25:43,763 --> 01:25:45,682
I can already tell.
He knows what the numbers are

1587
01:25:45,765 --> 01:25:47,433
and where the equal sign goes.

1588
01:25:47,517 --> 01:25:50,270
If that's what he was going for,
he could've made it more confusing…

1589
01:25:50,353 --> 01:25:53,439
Exactly, because the equal sign,
it's in a little too obvious of a spot.

1590
01:26:00,029 --> 01:26:02,323
See, this is why he looks so strong.

1591
01:26:02,407 --> 01:26:04,200
It's like he knows
exactly what he's doing.

1592
01:26:04,284 --> 01:26:05,702
-Mmm.
-Real confident guy.

1593
01:26:05,785 --> 01:26:07,328
Place your answer in front of your screen.

1594
01:26:10,373 --> 01:26:12,792
Whoa, nine to the power of one.

1595
01:26:12,876 --> 01:26:15,628
Wait, is it?
Is it nine to the power of one?

1596
01:26:16,254 --> 01:26:19,299
It could also be 91 times nine
to the power of zero.

1597
01:26:21,426 --> 01:26:23,303
To see if there were any repeats,

1598
01:26:23,386 --> 01:26:25,388
this time I put in multiples
of the same numbers.

1599
01:26:25,471 --> 01:26:27,307
There's always a chance
he could use duplicates,

1600
01:26:27,390 --> 01:26:29,517
so this turn I wanted to try
and suss that out.

1601
01:26:29,601 --> 01:26:31,269
Here are your color clues.

1602
01:26:35,899 --> 01:26:38,735
You have five minutes
to come up with your answer.

1603
01:26:38,818 --> 01:26:42,530
It was 91. He could solve it on this turn.

1604
01:26:43,323 --> 01:26:44,741
Five greens this time.

1605
01:26:44,824 --> 01:26:47,744
Even the zero in front of the "equals 91"
he guessed right.

1606
01:26:47,827 --> 01:26:50,997
Which means now
he could figure out the exponent is zero,

1607
01:26:51,080 --> 01:26:53,708
plus he already knows
the whole thing starts with a nine.

1608
01:26:53,791 --> 01:26:55,585
He could win it all on the next attempt.

1609
01:26:55,668 --> 01:26:57,837
It is 91 times nine to the power of zero.

1610
01:26:57,921 --> 01:26:59,547
-You called it.
-He's got over half of it solved.

1611
01:26:59,631 --> 01:27:00,965
-This is it.
-We're coming up on the end.

1612
01:27:12,018 --> 01:27:13,561
He has to know…

1613
01:27:13,645 --> 01:27:16,022
that anything to the power of zero
is one, right?

1614
01:27:16,105 --> 01:27:17,565
Actually, I don't think
Dong-min knows that.

1615
01:27:17,649 --> 01:27:20,276
-Does he seriously not know?
-Yeah, there's a chance he doesn't.

1616
01:27:20,360 --> 01:27:22,570
Even if he doesn't, he could still
just shift things around

1617
01:27:22,654 --> 01:27:23,655
until he gets the answer.

1618
01:27:23,738 --> 01:27:25,949
And he could take a guess
and go, "Oh, is this a one?"

1619
01:27:26,032 --> 01:27:27,033
And then that's the end of it.

1620
01:27:27,116 --> 01:27:29,702
I still can't even figure out
Dong-min's equation.

1621
01:27:29,786 --> 01:27:30,995
His is pretty random,

1622
01:27:31,079 --> 01:27:33,998
whereas Kyung-lyul's only has
a few numbers and an exponent, so…

1623
01:27:34,582 --> 01:27:36,125
Sixty seconds remain.

1624
01:27:43,716 --> 01:27:45,176
Thirty seconds remain.

1625
01:27:51,808 --> 01:27:53,935
Please place your answer
in front of your screen.

1626
01:27:54,811 --> 01:27:56,062
Oh, come on…

1627
01:28:09,617 --> 01:28:10,868
So, uh…

1628
01:28:10,952 --> 01:28:14,998
Yeah, I was not aware that
any number to the power of zero is one.

1629
01:28:15,081 --> 01:28:18,084
Ugh. Should've paid
more attention in class.

1630
01:28:21,587 --> 01:28:24,757
Right now, I know
where the four, the two, the five,

1631
01:28:24,841 --> 01:28:26,217
and the plus sign are.

1632
01:28:26,301 --> 01:28:27,552
The past three tries,

1633
01:28:27,635 --> 01:28:30,430
I've been trying the exponent sign
in a few different spots,

1634
01:28:30,513 --> 01:28:32,348
but they've all been wrong.

1635
01:28:32,432 --> 01:28:35,685
So the only way it could work
is if it was two to the power of five.

1636
01:28:35,768 --> 01:28:39,772
It'd have to be two to the power of five,
plus something, equals 40-something.

1637
01:28:39,856 --> 01:28:42,275
Two to the power of five on its own is 32,

1638
01:28:42,358 --> 01:28:44,861
so the singular one in the equation
that I couldn't pin down

1639
01:28:44,944 --> 01:28:46,404
would have to go here.

1640
01:28:46,487 --> 01:28:48,406
And that only leaves five and seven.

1641
01:28:54,245 --> 01:28:55,913
Here are your color clues.

1642
01:29:01,169 --> 01:29:03,463
Hyun Kyung-lyul, you are correct.

1643
01:29:06,007 --> 01:29:08,634
<i>The final winner</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan

1644
01:29:08,718 --> 01:29:10,553
<i>is Hyun Kyung-lyul.</i>

1645
01:29:16,225 --> 01:29:17,685
Round of applause, people.

1646
01:29:19,228 --> 01:29:20,438
Argh!

1647
01:29:24,400 --> 01:29:26,027
Goddamn it, I'm tearing up.

1648
01:29:26,110 --> 01:29:28,821
-I always believed in you, bud.
-Thank you, thank you.

1649
01:29:30,281 --> 01:29:32,075
-Bro, the equal sign.
-That was freaking amazing.

1650
01:29:32,158 --> 01:29:33,576
The equal sign came in clutch. Congrats.

1651
01:29:33,659 --> 01:29:36,120
-Oh, my God, you're a freakin' genius.
-Wow.

1652
01:29:36,204 --> 01:29:38,456
This victory doesn't feel
like I dominated.

1653
01:29:38,539 --> 01:29:42,251
I just never gave up, and narrowly
managed to beat each player one by one,

1654
01:29:42,335 --> 01:29:44,170
slowly working my way up to the top.

1655
01:29:44,253 --> 01:29:47,799
And every step of the way, I learned
what I could from all of my opponents,

1656
01:29:47,882 --> 01:29:49,133
growing stronger each day.

1657
01:29:49,217 --> 01:29:51,177
The victory's 'cause of them.

1658
01:29:51,260 --> 01:29:53,054
-You're amazing.
-Well done, my friend.

1659
01:29:53,137 --> 01:29:54,222
Really nice job.

1660
01:29:54,305 --> 01:29:56,099
Well, he earned it.

1661
01:29:56,182 --> 01:29:59,310
Yeah, I've got to admit defeat.
He played well.

1662
01:29:59,394 --> 01:30:02,688
And this loss feels like a sign
from above to learn from my mistakes,

1663
01:30:02,772 --> 01:30:05,233
challenge myself again, and do better.

1664
01:30:05,316 --> 01:30:07,360
If I ever get
another opportunity like this,

1665
01:30:07,443 --> 01:30:11,155
I'm gonna tackle it with the mindset
of a challenger, not a champion.

1666
01:30:11,239 --> 01:30:12,949
And I'm never gonna lose again.

1667
01:30:13,825 --> 01:30:17,286
You know, now that it's over,
I actually feel pretty relieved.

1668
01:30:17,370 --> 01:30:19,497
And I gotta say, in the second game…

1669
01:30:20,873 --> 01:30:24,127
…yeah, in the fifth round,
I was certain I had won.

1670
01:30:25,044 --> 01:30:28,506
Like, I was so sure of my victory
that I was thinking to myself,

1671
01:30:28,589 --> 01:30:31,050
"All right, what am I gonna say
in my victory speech?"

1672
01:30:32,552 --> 01:30:34,637
That's what was going through my head.

1673
01:30:34,720 --> 01:30:37,348
But I guess I lost
because I didn't really…

1674
01:30:37,432 --> 01:30:41,310
I didn't follow my own maxim,
the one I'm always

1675
01:30:41,394 --> 01:30:43,020
saying to each of you guys.

1676
01:30:43,104 --> 01:30:44,981
"It's not over until it's over."

1677
01:30:45,857 --> 01:30:48,443
But now, I kind of feel like
a weight's been lifted.

1678
01:30:48,526 --> 01:30:52,905
I hope the fan base of survival shows
like these keeps on growing,

1679
01:30:52,989 --> 01:30:54,991
'cause I wanna see
more great shows like this,

1680
01:30:55,074 --> 01:30:57,952
and I want <i>The Devil's Plan</i>
to continue for a long time.

1681
01:30:59,704 --> 01:31:01,414
-Thank you!
-Respect!

1682
01:31:01,497 --> 01:31:02,915
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul is the winner</i>

1683
01:31:02,999 --> 01:31:06,294
<i>and will take home</i>
<i>the final prize of 200 million won.</i>

1684
01:31:06,377 --> 01:31:08,379
-Congratulations, my man.
-All the kudos, bro.

1685
01:31:08,463 --> 01:31:09,672
Wow, that was incredible. Respect.

1686
01:31:09,755 --> 01:31:11,299
-Well played.
-Great work.

1687
01:31:13,050 --> 01:31:14,469
Uh, first of all,

1688
01:31:15,052 --> 01:31:17,263
I'd like to dedicate this honor
to my beloved wife

1689
01:31:17,346 --> 01:31:19,182
who's supported me in every way possible.

1690
01:31:19,265 --> 01:31:20,600
I knew he'd credit his wife.

1691
01:31:20,683 --> 01:31:23,060
You know, as a guy in his 40s
working an office job,

1692
01:31:23,144 --> 01:31:25,396
I live a bit of an ordinary life,

1693
01:31:25,480 --> 01:31:28,316
but getting to be a part
of something like this, well, it's…

1694
01:31:28,399 --> 01:31:30,902
It's pretty extraordinary for me.

1695
01:31:30,985 --> 01:31:33,196
So I'm grateful…
I'm so grateful to the show

1696
01:31:33,279 --> 01:31:35,239
for giving me the chance to show

1697
01:31:35,323 --> 01:31:37,783
all the other ordinary
office workers out there

1698
01:31:37,867 --> 01:31:39,535
-you could do this too.
-Hear, hear.

1699
01:31:39,619 --> 01:31:41,496
If you unleash the passion
hidden within you,

1700
01:31:41,579 --> 01:31:43,664
you really can achieve anything.

1701
01:31:43,748 --> 01:31:46,000
'Cause look… I'm the winner!

1702
01:31:50,254 --> 01:31:52,215
<i>With Hyun Kyung-lyul's victory,</i>

1703
01:31:52,298 --> 01:31:55,551
<i>all the games of </i>The Devil's Plan
<i>have come to an end.</i>

1704
01:31:55,635 --> 01:31:59,055
<i>Thank you to all the players</i>
<i>who took part.</i>

1705
01:32:00,223 --> 01:32:01,849
-The game's over!
-Thanks, everyone.

1706
01:32:03,768 --> 01:32:05,561
-Well done!
-Nice work, everyone!

1707
01:32:05,645 --> 01:32:07,396
What does
<i>The Devil's Plan </i>mean to me?

1708
01:32:07,480 --> 01:32:09,524
It's brought me glory, and also…

1709
01:32:09,607 --> 01:32:12,443
It's given me my first
proper experience of defeat, but…

1710
01:32:12,527 --> 01:32:14,570
Not everyone
gets the chance to do stuff like this.

1711
01:32:14,654 --> 01:32:16,531
Now that
I've been through <i>The Devil's Plan</i>…

1712
01:32:16,614 --> 01:32:19,325
It feels like a story
about a life-changing experience.

1713
01:32:19,408 --> 01:32:21,536
For me, it's a place
I've learned more about life.

1714
01:32:21,619 --> 01:32:24,413
About the passion
and desire I thought I'd forgotten.

1715
01:32:25,373 --> 01:32:27,375
These seven days have
given me a chance to see

1716
01:32:27,458 --> 01:32:30,169
if my competitive spirit
can still be ignited.

1717
01:32:30,253 --> 01:32:32,338
It made me think,
"If I could do this again,

1718
01:32:32,421 --> 01:32:34,048
I'd really give it everything."

1719
01:32:34,131 --> 01:32:36,384
I'm grateful for the opportunity
to challenge myself.

1720
01:32:36,467 --> 01:32:38,344
Ah, in the week I've spent here…

1721
01:32:38,427 --> 01:32:40,596
Every day, weird as this sounds,

1722
01:32:40,680 --> 01:32:43,432
I've been hungry, but happy,
and I've been cold, but warm.

1723
01:32:43,516 --> 01:32:45,518
All my time here really showed me

1724
01:32:45,601 --> 01:32:48,771
that you've got to just
live life to the fullest.

1725
01:32:48,854 --> 01:32:51,607
'Cause it's not about surviving.
It's about actually living.

1726
01:32:51,691 --> 01:32:54,819
It's been a great opportunity
to reflect on myself.

1727
01:32:54,902 --> 01:32:58,948
It's a place that genuinely
helped me grow as a person.

1728
01:32:59,031 --> 01:33:00,700
Getting to play in this world,

1729
01:33:00,783 --> 01:33:03,786
having as much fun as I did, like,
more than I could've dreamed…

1730
01:33:03,869 --> 01:33:06,205
I'm happy
that I've learned as much as I have.

1731
01:33:06,289 --> 01:33:09,375
I love that it's made me feel
this many emotions again,

1732
01:33:09,458 --> 01:33:10,626
the good and the bad.

1733
01:33:10,710 --> 01:33:13,629
This place feels like
a second home that I'll miss forever.

1734
01:33:13,713 --> 01:33:16,048
Yeah, definitely got a sense of regret.

1735
01:33:16,132 --> 01:33:17,717
It was everything to me,

1736
01:33:17,800 --> 01:33:20,219
and it's something
that I put my full force into.

1737
01:33:20,303 --> 01:33:21,929
It was an honor to be a part of that.

1738
01:33:22,013 --> 01:33:24,307
I'll never forget
how much I enjoyed myself this week.

1739
01:33:24,390 --> 01:33:26,684
It was an awesome time, to put it lightly.

1740
01:33:26,767 --> 01:33:29,228
I really enjoyed playing all these games.

1741
01:33:30,229 --> 01:33:31,772
Okay, last one, everybody.

1742
01:33:31,856 --> 01:33:33,941
One, two, three!

1743
01:33:34,025 --> 01:33:35,693
Thank you!

1744
01:33:35,776 --> 01:33:37,069
Hell yeah.

1745
01:33:37,153 --> 01:33:39,572
And that's a wrap! Let's get outta here!
